* [[Mary Jo Catlett]] as [[Mrs. Puff]]
* [[Lori Alan]] as [[Pearl Krabs]]

Most one-off and background characters are voiced by [[Dee Bradley Baker]], [[Sirena Irwin]], [[Bob Joles]], [[Mark Fite]] and [[Thomas F. Wilson]].<ref>{{cite web |title=SpongeBob SquarePants – Full Cast and Crew |url=https://www.tvguide.com/tvshows/spongebob-squarepants/cast/1000085609/ |access-date=January 30, 2026 |website=TV Guide}}</ref>

==== Casting ====
As Hillenburg, Drymon and Hill were writing the pilot episode, Hillenburg was also conducting auditions for voice actors.<ref name="OralHistory" /><ref name="Fagerbakkevoice">{{cite web |last=Liu |first=Ed |date=November 11, 2013 |title=Being Patrick Star: Toonzone Interviews Bill Fagerbakke on ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' |url=http://www.toonzone.net/2013/11/patrick-star-toonzone-interviews-bill-fagerbakke-spongebob-squarepants/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131219000346/http://www.toonzone.net/2013/11/patrick-star-toonzone-interviews-bill-fagerbakke-spongebob-squarepants/ |archive-date=December 19, 2013 |access-date=March 28, 2014 |work=Toon Zone}}</ref> Tom Kenny had previously worked with Hillenburg on ''Rocko's Modern Life,'' and Hillenburg liked the voice he had used for a minor character.<ref name="Radio" /><ref>{{cite web |last1=Orlando |first1=Dana |date=March 17, 2003 |title=SpongeBob: the excitable, absorbent star of Bikini Bottom |url=http://www.sptimes.com/2003/03/17/Xpress/SpongeBob__the_excita.shtml |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170320075638/http://www.sptimes.com/2003/03/17/Xpress/SpongeBob__the_excita.shtml |archive-date=March 20, 2017 |access-date=August 6, 2019 |work=St. Petersburg Times}}</ref> He approached Kenny about voicing SpongeBob, but Kenny had forgotten how to perform the voice; Hillenburg used a video clip from ''Rocko'' to remind him.<ref name="Radio" /><ref name="OralHistory" /> Nickelodeon insisted on auditioning more actors for the role of SpongeBob, but Hillenburg turned them down.<ref name="OralHistory" /> According to Kenny, Hillenburg described SpongeBob to him as childlike and naive, somewhere between an adult and a child.<ref name="OralHistory" /> The casting crew wanted SpongeBob to have an annoying laugh in the tradition of [[Popeye]] and [[Woody Woodpecker]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Morales |first=Tatiana |date=December 30, 2002 |title=SpongeBob's Alter Ego |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/spongebobs-alter-ego/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130921223746/http://www.cbsnews.com/stories/2002/12/27/earlyshow/leisure/celebspot/main534521.shtml?source=search_story |archive-date=September 21, 2013 |access-date=November 8, 2008 |work=[[CBS News]]}}</ref>

