During Bill Fagerbakke's audition for Patrick, Hillenburg played him a portion of Kenny's performance as SpongeBob to serve as a counterpoint.<ref name="Fagerbakkevoice" /> Whenever Patrick is angry, Fagerbakke models his performance on the actress [[Shelley Winters]].{{sfn |Banks |2004 |page=33}}<ref name="FagerbakkeInt">{{cite web |last=Douglas |first=Patrick |date=January 14, 2008 |title="Transformers:Animated"/"Spongebob Squarepants"/"Coach" – Bill Fagerbakke (2008) |url=http://www.thecultureshock.com/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=802&Itemid=44 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110716231329/http://www.thecultureshock.com/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=802&Itemid=44 |archive-date=July 16, 2011 |access-date=May 22, 2013 |work=The Culture Shock}}</ref> Rodger Bumpass described his character Squidward as "a very nasally, monotone kind of guy." Bumpass found Squidward interesting due to his range of emotions, including frustration, apoplexy and sarcasm.<ref name="Bumpass">{{cite web |last=Reardon |first=Samantha |date=September 8, 2013 |title=Rodger Bumpass is Squidward Tentacles |url=http://georgiastatesignal.com/rodger-bumpass-is-squidward-tentacles/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140328111302/http://georgiastatesignal.com/rodger-bumpass-is-squidward-tentacles/ |archive-date=March 28, 2014 |access-date=March 28, 2014 |work=[[The Signal (college newspaper)|The Signal]]}}</ref> Hillenburg modeled Mr. Krabs after his former manager at a seafood restaurant, whose strong [[Maine accent]] reminded Hillenburg of a pirate.<ref name="minipage">{{cite web |date=July 12, 2015 |title=What a Sponge! |url=http://nieonline.com/coloradonie/downloads/minipage/minipage7.15.15.pdf |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170415104043/http://nieonline.com/coloradonie/downloads/minipage/minipage7.15.15.pdf |archive-date=April 15, 2017 |work=[[The Mini Page]] |publisher=[[Andrews McMeel Universal]]}}</ref> Clancy Brown added a slight [[Scottish accent]] to the "piratey" voice of the character.{{sfn |Beck |2013 |pp=86–88}}

When the series began, Mr. Lawrence voiced a variety of minor characters, including Plankton, who was initially only meant to appear in one episode.<ref name="MrLawrenceInt">{{cite interview |last=Lawrence |first=Doug |subject-link=Mr. Lawrence |interviewer=[[Thomas F. Wilson]] |title=Big Pop Fun #22: Mr. Lawrence |medium=Podcast |url=http://hwcdn.libsyn.com/p/8/0/b/80ba5601f7d09e93/BPF22_Mr._Lawrence.mp3?c_id=4442198&expiration=1396087344&hwt=77616525493ac25efba1ba04f5cd6efc |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191227221747/http://hwcdn.libsyn.com/p/8/0/b/80ba5601f7d09e93/BPF22_Mr._Lawrence.mp3?c_id=4442198&expiration=1396087344&hwt=77616525493ac25efba1ba04f5cd6efc |archive-date=December 27, 2019 |format=mp3 |publisher=[[Nerdist Industries]] |date=April 2012}}</ref><ref name="OralHistory" /> According to Lawrence, Nickelodeon executives wanted Hillenburg to [[Stunt casting|stunt-cast]] a celebrity for Plankton, but he declined.<ref name="MrLawrenceInt" /> Talley and Mr. Lawrence often improvise the dialogue of Plankton and Karen; Lawrence said improvisation is his favorite part of the job.<ref>{{cite interview |last=Lawrence |first=Doug |subject-link=Mr. Lawrence |interviewer=Andy Goodman |title=Andy interviews Mr Lawrence aka "the Slasher" |url=http://www.nicknz.co.nz/SpongeBob/Backstage/Blog/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100611022322/http://www.nicknz.co.nz/SpongeBob/Backstage/Blog/ |archive-date=June 11, 2010 |work=[[Nickelodeon (New Zealand)|Nick NZ]] |date=2009}}</ref> Electronic sound effects are added to create a robotic sound when Karen speaks.<ref>{{cite video |title=F.U.N. backstage featurette, Nautical Nonsense |date=2002 |medium=DVD |publisher=[[Paramount Home Media Distribution|Paramount Home Entertainment]] |people=Lawrence, Doug}}</ref>
