=== Streaming ===
==== United States ====
In May 2013, a deal between [[Netflix]] and Nickelodeon's parent company [[Viacom (2005–2019)|Viacom]] expired, which resulted in shows such as ''SpongeBob'' and ''Dora the Explorer'' being removed from Netflix in the United States, although ''SpongeBob'' continues to be available on Netflix in certain other regions.''<ref name="over">{{cite web |last=Poggi |first=Jeanine |date=June 4, 2013 |title=Netflix Deal Over, Viacom Takes ''Dora'' and ''SpongeBob'' to Amazon Prime |url=https://adage.com/article/media/amazon-signs-exclusive-deal-stream-viacom-shows/241846 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130610182358/https://adage.com/article/media/amazon-signs-exclusive-deal-stream-viacom-shows/241846 |archive-date=June 10, 2013 |access-date=July 31, 2020 |work=[[Ad Age]]}}</ref>''<ref name="NotRenew">{{cite news |last=Wallenstein |first=Andrew |date=April 22, 2013 |title=Viacom and Netflix to Scale Down SVOD Deal |url=https://variety.com/2013/digital/news/viacom-and-netflix-to-scale-down-svod-deal-1200407086/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201007110309/https://variety.com/2013/digital/news/viacom-and-netflix-to-scale-down-svod-deal-1200407086/ |archive-date=October 7, 2020 |access-date=May 26, 2013 |newspaper=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Roettgers |first=Janko |date=May 23, 2013 |title=Adios, Dora: Netflix is starting to take Viacom shows offline |url=http://paidcontent.org/2013/05/23/no-more-dora-spongebob-on-netflix/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130607183520/http://paidcontent.org/2013/05/23/no-more-dora-spongebob-on-netflix/ |archive-date=June 7, 2013 |access-date=May 26, 2013 |publisher=[[paidContent]]}}</ref><ref name="Flixboss">{{Cite web |title=Is ''SpongeBob SquarePants (1999)'' on Netflix? |url=https://ca.flixboss.com/series/spongebob-squarepants-70155547 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181219090848/https://ca.flixboss.com/series/spongebob-squarepants-70155547 |archive-date=December 19, 2018 |access-date=July 31, 2020 |website=Flixboss}}</ref> In June of that year, Viacom announced a $200 million multi-year licensing agreement which would move its programs, including ''SpongeBob'', to [[Amazon.com|Amazon]].<ref>{{cite news |date=June 4, 2013 |title=Dora, SpongeBob Swap Sides in Fickle Web-Video World |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB10001424127887324423904578525044270830934 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201008171408/https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB10001424127887324423904578525044270830934 |archive-date=October 8, 2020 |access-date=June 5, 2013 |newspaper=[[The Wall Street Journal]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Moscariloto |first=Angela |date=June 4, 2013 |title=Amazon Inks Streaming Deal for Viacom Shows Like Dora, SpongeBob |url=https://www.pcmag.com/article2/0,2817,2419901,00.asp |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181219090858/https://www.pcmag.com/article2/0,2817,2419901,00.asp |archive-date=December 19, 2018 |access-date=June 5, 2013 |magazine=[[PCMag.com]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Barr |first=Alistair |date=June 4, 2013 |title=Amazon writes biggest streaming video check for Dora, SpongeBob |url=http://www.denverpost.com/technology/ci_23385278/amazon-writes-biggest-streaming-video-check-dora-spongebob |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304082026/http://www.denverpost.com/technology/ci_23385278/amazon-writes-biggest-streaming-video-check-dora-spongebob |archive-date=March 4, 2016 |access-date=June 5, 2013 |work=[[Denver Post]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=June 4, 2013 |title=Amazon swipes SpongeBob from Netflix in most expensive deal yet |url=http://www.mercurynews.com/business/ci_23385964/amazon-swipes-spongebob-from-netflix-most-expensive-deal |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130606165437/http://www.mercurynews.com/business/ci_23385964/amazon-swipes-spongebob-from-netflix-most-expensive-deal |archive-date=June 6, 2013 |access-date=June 5, 2013 |work=[[The Mercury News]]}}</ref> ''SpongeBob'' was available on [[Hulu]] from 2012 until 2016, and on [[Amazon Prime Video]] after the Netflix deal ended.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Rome |first=Emily |date=October 9, 2012 |title=Nickelodeon shows now available to watch on Hulu Plus |url=https://ew.com/article/2012/10/09/nickelodeon-hulu-plus/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150215154106/https://ew.com/article/2012/10/09/nickelodeon-hulu-plus/ |archive-date=February 15, 2015 |access-date=July 31, 2020 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref><ref name="over" /> In 2020, ''SpongeBob'' became available on [[Paramount+]].<ref name="Deadline-KK-CBS">{{cite web |last=Hayes |first=Dade |date=July 30, 2020 |title=''SpongeBob SquarePants'' Spinoff ''Kamp Koral'' Shifts To CBS All Access As Nickelodeon Library Shows Arrive |url=https://deadline.com/2020/07/spongebob-squarepants-spinoff-kamp-koral-shifts-to-cbs-all-access-as-nickelodeon-library-shows-arrive-1202998734/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200730191630/https://deadline.com/2020/07/spongebob-squarepants-spinoff-kamp-koral-shifts-to-cbs-all-access-as-nickelodeon-library-shows-arrive-1202998734/ |archive-date=July 30, 2020 |access-date=July 30, 2020 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref name="TFC-PR-CBS">{{cite press release |title=ViacomCBS Debuts Expanded and Enhanced CBS All Access |date=July 30, 2020 |publisher=[[CBS]] |url=http://thefutoncritic.com/news/2020/07/30/viacomcbs-debuts-expanded-and-enhanced-cbs-all-access-370101/20200730cbs01/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]] |access-date=July 31, 2020 |archive-date=April 18, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210418054317/https://www.google-analytics.com/ga.js |url-status=live }}</ref> As of June 2025, the first six seasons of the series are available on Amazon, and the first 14 seasons are available on Paramount+.<ref>{{cite web |title=''SpongeBob SquarePants'' – Where to Stream and Watch |url=https://decider.com/show/spongebob-squarepants/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141013042936/https://decider.com/show/spongebob-squarepants/ |archive-date=October 13, 2014 |access-date=June 12, 2025 |work=[[New York Post#Website|Decider]]}}</ref>

