ration.html |archive-date=January 24, 2010 |publisher=[[Annie Award]]}}</ref><ref name="Annie38">{{cite web |title=38th Annual Annie Nominations |url=http://www.annieawards.org/consideration.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110906082547/http://www.annieawards.org/consideration.html |archive-date=September 6, 2011 |access-date=May 21, 2013 |publisher=[[Annie Award]]}}</ref><ref name="Annie401">{{cite web |date=December 4, 2012 |title=Annie Award Nominations — A Real Race For Once |url=http://thefilmexperience.net/blog/2012/12/4/annie-award-nominations-a-real-race-for-once.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130323062852/http://thefilmexperience.net/blog/2012/12/4/annie-award-nominations-a-real-race-for-once.html |archive-date=March 23, 2013 |access-date=April 13, 2013 |publisher=TheFilmExperience.net}}</ref><ref name="Annie402">{{cite news |date=February 2, 2013 |title=40th Annie Award nominees and winners list |url=https://www.latimes.com/entertainment/envelope/la-xpm-2013-feb-02-la-et-mn-40th-annie-award-nominations-winners-list-20130202-story.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180115171020/http://articles.latimes.com/2013/feb/02/entertainment/la-et-mn-40th-annie-award-nominations-winners-list-20130202 |archive-date=January 15, 2018 |access-date=May 23, 2013 |newspaper=[[Los Angeles Times]]}}</ref>}} and two [[British Academy Children's Awards|BAFTA Children's Awards]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Children's in 2007 |url=http://awards.bafta.org/award/2007/childrens |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160305074253/http://awards.bafta.org/award/2007/childrens |archive-date=March 5, 2016 |access-date=April 1, 2014 |work=[[British Academy Children's Awards]] |publisher=[[British Academy of Film and Television Arts]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Children's in 2012 |url=http://awards.bafta.org/award/2012/childrens |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160305082901/http://awards.bafta.org/award/2012/childrens/ |archive-date=March 5, 2016 |access-date=April 1, 2014 |work=[[British Academy Children's Awards]] |publisher=[[British Academy of Film and Television Arts]]}}</ref> In 2006, ''[[IGN]]'' ranked ''SpongeBob'' the 15th best animated series of all time, and in 2013 it ranked the series 12th on its list of the Top 25 Animated Series for Adults.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{cite web |date=September 28, 2006 |title=15. ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2006/09/29/top-25-primetime-animated-series-of-all-time?page=3 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120923030609/http://www.ign.com/articles/2006/09/29/top-25-primetime-animated-series-of-all-time?page=3 |archive-date=September 23, 2012 |access-date=December 31, 2013 |website=[[IGN]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=July 15, 2013 |title=The Top 25 Animated Shows for Adults |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2013/07/15/top-25-animated-shows-for-adults?page=3 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130723190001/https://www.ign.com/articles/2013/07/15/top-25-animated-shows-for-adults?page=3 |archive-date=July 23, 2013 |access-date=December 4, 2013 |website=[[IGN]]}}</ref><ref name="IGN">{{cite web |title=Nickelodeon: ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' |url=http://uk.tv.ign.com/top-100-animated-tv-series/15.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120620010829/http://uk.tv.ign.com/top-100-animated-tv-series/15.html |archive-date=June 20, 2012 |access-date=December 29, 2012 |website=[[IGN]]}}</ref>}}

In 2007, ''Time'' television critic James Poniewozik ranked ''SpongeBob'' among the best 100 television series of all time.<ref name="alltime100">{{cite magazine |author=Poniewozik, James |date=August 14, 2007 |title=All-TIME 100 TV shows: ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' |url=http://entertainment.time.com/2007/09/06/the-100-best-tv-shows-of-all-time/slide/spongebob-squarepants-2/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111022130006/http://entertainment.time.com/2007/09/06/the-100-best-tv-shows-of-all-time/slide/spongebob-squarepants-2/ |archive-date=October 22, 2011 |access-date=May 11, 2013 |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|Time]]}}</ref> Viewers of UK television network [[Channel 4]] voted ''SpongeBob'' the 28th Greatest Cartoon in a 2004 poll.<ref>{{cite web |title=The 100 Greatest Cartoons – Results |url=http://www.channel4.com/entertainment/tv/microsites/G/greatest/cartoons/results.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090520014452/http://www.channel4.com/entertainment/tv/microsites/G/greatest/cartoons/results.html |archive-date=May 20, 2009 |publisher=[[Channel 4]].com}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=The 100 Greatest Cartoons – The Show |url=http://www.channel4.com/entertainment/tv/microsites/G/greatest/cartoons/index.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090422100525/http://www.channel4.com/entertainment/tv/microsites/G/greatest/cartoons/index.html |archive-date=April 22, 2009 |publisher=Channel 4.com}}</ref> In 2013, the publication ranked ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' eighth on its list of the Greatest TV Cartoons of All Time.<ref>{{cite web |date=September 24, 2013 |title=TV Guide Magazine's 60 Greatest Cartoons of All Time |url=https://www.tvguide.com/News/Greatest-Cartoons-TV-Guide-Magazine-1071203.aspx |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180710095501/https://www.tvguide.com/news/greatest-cartoons-tv-guide-magazine-1071203/ |archive-date=July 10, 2018 |access-date=December 4, 2013 |work=[[TV Guide]]}}</ref> Critics [[Alan Sepinwall]] and [[Matt Zoller Seitz]] ranked ''SpongeBob'' as the 22nd greatest American television series of all time in their 2016 book ''[[TV (The Book): Two Experts Pick the Greatest American Shows of All Time|TV (The Book)]]''.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{cite news |last1=Champagne |first1=Christine |date=August 31, 2016 |title=Two Critics Pick The All-Time Best TV Shows. And They Know You Already Hate Their List |url=https://www.fastcocreate.com/3063291/two-critics-pick-the-all-time-best-tv-shows-and-they-know-you-already-hate-their-list |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160915081700/https://www.fastcocreate.com/3063291/two-critics-pick-the-all-time-best-tv-shows-and-they-know-you-already-hate-their-list |archive-date=September 15, 2016 |access-date=March 9, 2026 |website=[[Fast Company (magazine)#Online|Co.Create]] |publisher=[[Mansueto Ventures]], LLC}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=July 14, 2009 |title=From Bikini Bottom to pop icon; SpongeBob turns 10 |url=http://in.reuters.com/article/television-spongebob-idINN1319626220090713 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151226125203/http://in.reuters.com/article/television-spongebob-idINN1319626220090713 |archive-date=December 26, 2015 |access-date=April 28, 2013 |work=Reuters}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Seitz |first1=Matt Zoller |author-link=Matt Zoller Seitz |last2=Sepinwall |first2=Alan |author2-link=Alan Sepinwall |date=September 1, 2016 |title=Why 'Deadwood' Is a Top-10 TV Show of All Time |url=https://theringer.com/deadwood-hbo-tv-the-book-dadb4007790e#.5f7cc3yte |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160902021203/https://theringer.com/deadwood-hbo-tv-the-book-dadb4007790e#.5f7cc3yte |archive-date=September 2, 2016 |access-date=September 2, 2016 |website=[[The Ringer (website)|The Ringer]] |publisher=Perfect Privacy, LLC}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Ashbrook |first1=Tom |date=September 9, 2016 |title=The Greatest American Television Shows, Ranked |url=http://www.wbur.org/onpoint/2016/09/09/the-greatest-american-television-shows-ranked |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160910141154/http://www.wbur.org/onpoint/2016/09/09/the-greatest-american-television-shows-ranked |archive-date=September 10, 2016 |access-date=September 10, 2016 |website=[[WBUR-FM|WBUR]] |publisher=WBUR}}</ref>}}

