===Spin-offs===
====''Kamp Koral: SpongeBob's Under Years''====
{{Main|Kamp Koral: SpongeBob's Under Years|l1 = ''Kamp Koral: SpongeBob's Under Years''}}

In June 2019, production began on a ''SpongeBob'' [[Spinoff (media)|spin-off]] series titled ''Kamp Koral: SpongeBob's Under Years.''<ref name="Spin-off">{{cite web |last=Zachary |first=Brandon |date=February 14, 2019 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants Spinoffs in the Works From Nickelodeon |url=https://www.cbr.com/spongebob-squarepants-spinoff-nickelodeon |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190215102741/https://www.cbr.com/spongebob-squarepants-spinoff-nickelodeon/ |archive-date=February 15, 2019 |access-date=February 14, 2019 |work=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref><ref name="The Futon Critic Kamp Koral" /> The plot focuses on the adventures of a 10-year-old SpongeBob and his friends at a camp in the Kelp Forest, where they spend the summer catching [[List of SpongeBob SquarePants characters#Jellyfish|jellyfish]], building campfires, and swimming in Lake Yuckymuck.<ref name="The Futon Critic Kamp Koral">{{cite press release |title=Nickelodeon Greenlights ''Kamp Koral'', Original Animated Spinoff of Hit Series ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' |date=June 4, 2019 |publisher=[[Nickelodeon]] |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2019/06/04/nickelodeon-greenlights-kamp-koral-original-animated-spinoff-of-hit-series-spongebob-squarepants-104415/20190604nickelodeon02/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]] |access-date=July 31, 2020 |archive-date=April 18, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210418054324/https://www.google-analytics.com/ga.js |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="announcement">{{cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=June 4, 2019 |title=''SpongeBob SquarePants'' CG-Animated Prequel Series ''Kamp Koral'' Greenlighted by Nickelodeon |url=https://deadline.com/2019/06/spongebob-squarepants-cg-animated-prequel-series-kamp-koral-greenlighted-nickelodeon-1202626441/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190927065041/https://deadline.com/2019/06/spongebob-squarepants-cg-animated-prequel-series-kamp-koral-greenlighted-nickelodeon-1202626441/ |archive-date=September 27, 2019 |access-date=July 31, 2020 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> The series served as a tie-in to the animated film ''[[The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge on the Run]]'' (2020), and had the same executive producers as ''SpongeBob:'' [[Marc Ceccarelli]], Jennie Monica, and Vincent Waller. ''Kamp Koral'' is produced using [[computer animation|computer-generated animation]] (CGI) rather than the digital ink and paint animation used for ''SpongeBob''.<ref name="announcement" /><ref>{{cite press release |title=Nickelodeon Announces Voice Cast for ''Kamp Koral: Spongebob's Under Years'', First-Ever ''Spongebob Squarepants'' Spinoff |date=February 19, 2020 |publisher=[[Nickelodeon]] |url=http://thefutoncritic.com/news/2020/02/19/nickelodeon-announces-voice-cast-for-kamp-koral-spongebobs-under-years-first-ever-spongebob-squarepants-spinoff-575101/20200219nickelodeon06/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]] |access-date=July 31, 2020 |archive-date=April 18, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210418054324/https://www.google-analytics.com/ga.js |url-status=live }}</ref> The series premiered on March&nbsp;4, 2021, and a second season debuted on July 10, 2024.<ref name="Sponge on Run Kamp Koral debut">{{cite web |last=Welk |first=Brian |date=January 28, 2021 |title=''SpongeBob Movie: Sponge on the Run'' to Debut on Paramount+ at March Launch |url=https://www.thewrap.com/spongebob-movie-sponge-on-the-run-release-paramount-plus-march-launch/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220712184829/https://www.thewrap.com/spongebob-movie-sponge-on-the-run-release-paramount-plus-march-launch/ |archive-date=July 12, 2022 |access-date=January 30, 2021 |work=[[TheWrap]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Danoff |first=Owen |date=June 20, 2024 |title=Kamp Koral: Spongebob's Under Years Season 2 Gets A Premiere Date & Series Art [EXCLUSIVE] |url=https://screenrant.com/kamp-koral-spongebobs-under-years-season-2-premiere-date-poster/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251208055229/https://screenrant.com/kamp-koral-spongebobs-under-years-season-2-premiere-date-poster/ |archive-date=December 8, 2025 |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=ScreenRant |language=en}}</ref><ref name="Deadline-KK-CBS" /><ref name="TFC-PR-CBS" />

====''The Patrick Star Show''====
{{Main|The Patrick Star Show|l1 = ''The Patrick Star Show''}}

On August&nbsp;10, 2020, it was reported that a Patrick Star talk show titled ''The Patrick Star Show'' was in development with a 13-episode order. Additionally, it was reported that the show would be similar to other talk shows such as ''[[The Larry Sanders Show]]'' and ''[[Comedy Bang! Bang! (TV series)|Comedy Bang! Bang!]]''<ref>{{cite web |author=Nellie Andreeva |date=August 10, 2020 |title=''SpongeBob SquarePants'' Spinoff Series ''The Patrick Star Show'' Set At Nickelodeon |url=https://deadline.com/2020/08/spongebob-squarepants-spinoff-series-the-patrick-star-show-set-nickelodeon-bill-fagerbakke-1203006633/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200811013253/https://deadline.com/2020/08/spongebob-squarepants-spinoff-series-the-patrick-star-show-set-nickelodeon-bill-fagerbakke-1203006633/ |archive-date=August 11, 2020 |access-date=August 10, 2020 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |author=Will Thorne |date=August 10, 2020 |title=''SpongeBob Squarepants'' Spinoff ''The Patrick Star Show'' in the Works to Nickelodeon |url=https://variety.com/2020/tv/news/spongebob-squarepants-spinoff-the-patrick-star-show-in-the-works-nickelodeon-1234730755/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200821053629/https://variety.com/2020/tv/news/spongebob-squarepants-spinoff-the-patrick-star-show-in-the-works-nickelodeon-1234730755/ |archive-date=August 21, 2020 |access-date=August 10, 2020 |work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> The series premiered on Nickelodeon on July&nbsp;9, 2021,<ref>{{cite web |author=Denise Petski |date=June 17, 2021 |title=Nickelodeon Unveils Trailers For ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' Spinoff ''The Patrick Star Show'' & ''Middlemost Post'', Sets Premiere Date |url=https://deadline.com/video/nickelodeon-trailers-spongebob-squarepants-spinoff-the-patrick-star-show-middleman-post-premiere-date/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210815234606/https://deadline.com/video/nickelodeon-trailers-spongebob-squarepants-spinoff-the-patrick-star-show-middleman-post-premiere-date/ |archive-date=August 15, 2021 |access-date=July 9, 2021 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> with the series set to be available on Paramount+ sometime in the future.<ref>{{cite web |author=Brian Steinberg |date=March 4, 2021 |title=Nickelodeon Set to Expand ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' With ''Patrick Star'' Series |url=https://variety.com/2021/tv/news/spongebob-squarepants-patrick-star-nickelodeon-paramount-plus-1234921485/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210304153703/https://variety.com/2021/tv/news/spongebob-squarepants-patrick-star-nickelodeon-paramount-plus-1234921485/ |archive-date=March 4, 2021 |access-date=March 4, 2021 |work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref>

Fans and former ''SpongeBob'' showrunner Paul Tibbitt criticized Nickelodeon when it [[Greenlight|greenlit]] spin-offs after the death of Hillenburg in 2018. In a [[Tweet (social media)|tweet]], Tibbit said Hillenburg would have hated the spin-offs, and he angrily admonished his former colleagues for working on them.<ref name="spinoffs">{{cite web |last=McKay |first=Karelle |date=March 7, 2021 |title='SpongeBob' Fans Are Not Excited For Patrick Star Spinoff, Feel It Dishonors Creator's Memory |url=https://www.thethings.com/spongebob-fans-are-not-excited-for-patrick-star-spinoff-feel-it-dishonors-creators-memory/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210417212526/https://www.thethings.com/spongebob-fans-are-not-excited-for-patrick-star-spinoff-feel-it-dishonors-creators-memory/ |archive-date=April 17, 2021 |access-date=March 31, 2021 |work=The Things}}</ref> In a 2009 interview, Hillenburg had been skeptical about the viability of spin-offs focusing on characters other than SpongeBob, and in 2017 Hillenburg's colleague [[Vincent Waller]] had stated that Hillenburg was against the creation of spin-offs.<ref>{{Cite web |last=White |first=Peter |date=October 27, 2009 |title=Spongebob Squarepants' creator Steve Hillenburg |url=https://www.lightreading.com/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210503080224/https://tbivision.com/2009/10/27/spongebob-squarepants-creator-steve-hillenburg/ |archive-date=May 3, 2021 |access-date=2026-02-27 |website=Television Business International |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |author=LeBlanc |first=Cameron |date=November 21, 2019 |title=Spongebob Is About to Become Nickelodeon's Marvel Universe Whether We Like it Or Not |url=https://news.yahoo.com/spongebob-creator-totally-opposed-spinoffs-172951877.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221103051633/https://news.yahoo.com/spongebob-creator-totally-opposed-spinoffs-172951877.html |archive-date=November 3, 2022 |access-date=November 3, 2022 |work=[[Yahoo! News]]}}</ref><ref name="ocean">{{Cite news |last=King |first=Darryn |date=August 13, 2019 |title=The Young Man and the Sea Sponge |url=https://longreads.com/2019/08/13/the-young-man-and-the-sea-sponge/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221103051629/https://longreads.com/2019/08/13/the-young-man-and-the-sea-sponge/ |archive-date=November 3, 2022 |access-date=June 22, 2021 |work=[[Longreads]]}}</ref>

===Super Bowl===
''SpongeBob SquarePants'' first appeared in the Super Bowl during the Super Bowl LIII halftime show, making a cameo appearance in the form of a short animation featuring Squidward, Mr. Krabs, Mrs. Puff, SpongeBob, and Patrick Star, which included footage of the Bikini Bottom band from the episode Band Geeks, before segueing into Travis Scott's section of the performance.<ref>{{cite news |last=Dill |first=Jason |date=December 21, 2018 |title=This is how a SpongeBob song would sound at this year's Super Bowl |url=https://www.miamiherald.com/sports/article223421025.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210211001657/https://www.miamiherald.com/sports/article223421025.html |archive-date=February 11, 2021 |access-date=February 13, 2024 |newspaper=[[The Miami Herald]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Donaghey |first1=River |last2=Schwartz |first2=Drew |date=November 30, 2018 |title=Over 50,000 Fans Want the Super Bowl to Play This 'SpongeBob' Song at Halftime |url=https://www.vice.com/en/article/petition-spongebob-song-superbowl-halftime-50000-signatures-sweet-victory-vgtrn/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190805194855/https://www.vice.com/en_us/article/nepddk/petition-spongebob-song-superbowl-halftime-50000-signatures-sweet-victory-vgtrn |archive-date=August 5, 2019 |access-date=February 13, 2024 |magazine=[[Vice (magazine)|Vice]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Hughes |first=William |date=November 30, 2018 |title=100,000 fans demand SpongeBob be allowed to play the half-time show at next year's Super Bowl |url=https://www.avclub.com/100-000-fans-demand-spongebob-be-allowed-to-play-the-ha-1830786621 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210423090614/https://news.avclub.com/100-000-fans-demand-spongebob-be-allowed-to-play-the-ha-1830786621 |archive-date=April 23, 2021 |access-date=February 13, 2024 |website=TheAVClub.com}}</ref><ref name="sb">{{Cite news |last=Radulovic |first=Petrana |date=February 3, 2019 |title=The Super Bowl halftime show just made tribute to Spongebob's creator |url=https://www.polygon.com/2019/2/3/18200897/spongebob-tribute-super-bowl-2019 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240202133016/https://www.polygon.com/2019/2/3/18200897/spongebob-tribute-super-bowl-2019 |archive-date=February 2, 2024 |access-date=February 13, 2024 |website=Polygon}}</ref> This led to fan outrage, as fans requested "Sweet Victory", the song featured in the episode, be played during the show, which ultimately did not occur.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Garrand |first=Danielle |date=February 4, 2019 |title=SpongeBob Squarepants: Fans have mixed reactions to Super Bowl 2019 halftime show appearance Sunday in Atlanta |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/spongebob-squarepants-fans-have-mixed-reactions-to-super-bowl-halftime-show-appearance-2019-02-03-atlanta/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230316204220/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/spongebob-squarepants-fans-have-mixed-reactions-to-super-bowl-halftime-show-appearance-2019-02-03-atlanta/ |archive-date=March 16, 2023 |access-date=January 22, 2025 |website=CBS News |language=en-US}}</ref> According to animator Nico Colaleo, the animation was completed in a few days.<ref>{{cite tweet |number=1092577409113632769 |user=NicoColaleo |title=Also in the short clip itself, the animation is different cuz this was literally done a week ago with only a few days to create ... |first=Nico |last=Colaleo |date=February 4, 2019 |access-date=February 13, 2024}}</ref>

On August{{nbsp}}1, 2023, [[CBS Sports]] announced that it would carry a [[NFL on Nickelodeon|youth-oriented alternate broadcast]] of Super Bowl LVIII on Nickelodeon, the first such broadcast for a Super Bowl.<ref>{{Cite web |date=August 1, 2023 |title=SpongeBob, slime to highlight Nickelodeon Super Bowl telecast |url=https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/38113170/spongebob-slime-highlight-nickelodeon-super-bowl-telecast |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230801225944/https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/38113170/spongebob-slime-highlight-nickelodeon-super-bowl-telecast |archive-date=August 1, 2023 |access-date=February 13, 2024 |website=ESPN.com}}</ref> Billed as ''Super Bowl{{nbsp}}LVIII: Live from Bikini Bottom'', the broadcast incorporated ''SpongeBob''-themed augmented reality effects and features (in addition to those seen on previous games aired by the network), and appearances by characters from the series (SpongeBob and Patrick acted as "analysts" alongside announcers [[Noah Eagle]] and [[Nate Burleson]], with Sandy Cheeks taking on "sideline reporter" duties).<ref>{{cite web |date=February 2024 |title=Nickelodeon and CBS Sports reveal details for slime-filed Super Bowl LVIII alternate telecast |url=https://www.paramountpressexpress.com/cbs-sports/shows/nfl-on-cbs/releases/?view=109170-nickelodeon-and-cbs-sports-reveal-details-for-slime-filled-super-bowl-lviii-alternate-telecast |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240203000720/https://www.paramountpressexpress.com/cbs-sports/shows/nfl-on-cbs/releases/?view=109170-nickelodeon-and-cbs-sports-reveal-details-for-slime-filled-super-bowl-lviii-alternate-telecast |archive-date=February 3, 2024 |access-date=February 12, 2024 |website=ParamountPress.com}}</ref>

===Comic books===
{{Main|SpongeBob Comics|l1 = ''SpongeBob Comics''}}

The 32-page bimonthly comic book series, ''[[SpongeBob Comics]]'', was announced in November 2010<ref name="Cartoon Phenom">{{cite web |date=November 11, 2010 |title='SpongeBob Comics': Cartoon Phenom Makes Comic Book Debut |url=http://www.icv2.com/articles/news/18770.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140408224711/http://www.icv2.com/articles/news/18770.html |archive-date=April 8, 2014 |access-date=April 8, 2014 |publisher=[[ICv2]]}}</ref> and debuted the following February.<ref name="comics on the way">{{cite web |last=Langshaw |first=Mark |date=November 11, 2010 |title='SpongeBob' comics on the way |url=http://www.digitalspy.com/comics/news/a287379/spongebob-comics-on-the-way.html#~oAM7JL2CzYw6EB |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101113023137/http://www.digitalspy.com/comics/news/a287379/spongebob-comics-on-the-way.html#~oAM7JL2CzYw6EB |archive-date=November 13, 2010 |access-date=April 8, 2014 |website=[[Digital Spy]]}}</ref> Before this, ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' comics had been published in ''[[Nickelodeon Magazine]]'',<ref name="Cartoon Phenom" /><ref name="Comics1">{{cite web |date=January 25, 2011 |title="SpongeBob SquarePants" Comic Debuts in February |url=http://www.comicbookresources.com/?page=article&id=30502 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110201210954/http://www.comicbookresources.com/?page=article&id=30502 |archive-date=February 1, 2011 |access-date=December 6, 2013 |website=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref><ref name="Comics2">{{cite web |last=Boom |first=Richard |date=January 25, 2011 |title=SpongeBob Comics #1 debuts from United Plankton Pictures |url=http://www.brokenfrontier.com/headlines/p/detail/spongebob-comics-1-debuts-from-united-plankton-pictures |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110128020705/http://www.brokenfrontier.com/headlines/p/detail/spongebob-comics-1-debuts-from-united-plankton-pictures |archive-date=January 28, 2011 |access-date=December 6, 2013 |publisher=[[Broken Frontier]]}}</ref> and episodes of the television series had been adapted by ''[[List of Tokyopop publications#Cine-Manga|Cine-Manga]]'',<ref name="Cartoon Phenom" /><ref>{{cite web |date=June 2, 2003 |title=Tokyopop Does Nickelodeon |url=https://icv2.com/articles/comics/view/2822/tokyopop-does-nickelodeon |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151125080642/https://icv2.com/articles/comics/view/2822/tokyopop-does-nickelodeon |archive-date=November 25, 2015 |access-date=August 25, 2019 |work=[[ICv2]]}}</ref> but ''SpongeBob Comics'' was the first American comic book series devoted solely to ''SpongeBob SquarePants''.<ref name="Cartoon Phenom" /><ref name="Comics1" /><ref name="Comics2" /> It also served as ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' creator Stephen Hillenburg's debut as a comic book author.<ref name="comics on the way" /><ref name="Comics1" /><ref name="Comics2" /> The series was published by Hillenburg's production company, [[United Plankton Pictures]], and distributed by [[Bongo Comics Group]].<ref name="Cartoon Phenom" /><ref name="Comics1" /><ref name="Comics2" /> Hillenburg described the stories from the comic books as "original and always true to the humor, characters, and universe of the SpongeBob SquarePants series." Leading up to the release of the series, Hillenburg said, "I'm hoping that fans will enjoy finally having a ''SpongeBob'' comic book from me."<ref name="Comics1" /><ref name="Comics2" />

Chris Duffy, the former senior editor of ''Nickelodeon Magazine'', serves as managing editor of ''SpongeBob Comics''.<ref name="Comics1" /><ref name="Comics2" /> Hillenburg and Duffy met with various cartoonists—including [[James Kochalka]], [[Hilary Barta]], [[Graham Annable]], Gregg Schigiel, and Jacob Chabot—to contribute to each issues.<ref name="Comics1" /><ref name="Comics2" /> Retired [[horror comics]] writer and artist [[Stephen R. Bissette]] returned to write a special Halloween issue in 2012, with [[Tony Millionaire]] and [[Al Jaffee]].<ref>{{cite web |author=Johnston, Rich |author-link=Rich Johnston |date=July 18, 2012 |title=Steve Bissette Returns To Comics With ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' |url=http://www.bleedingcool.com/2012/07/18/steve-bissette-returns-to-comics-with-spongebob-squarepants/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120719205226/http://www.bleedingcool.com/2012/07/18/steve-bissette-returns-to-comics-with-spongebob-squarepants/ |archive-date=July 19, 2012 |access-date=December 6, 2013 |publisher=[[Bleeding Cool]]}}</ref> In an interview with [[Tom Spurgeon]], Bissette said, "I've even broken my retirement to do one work-for-hire gig [for ''SpongeBob Comics''] so I could share everything about that kind of current job."<ref>{{cite web |author=Spurgeon, Tom |author-link=Tom Spurgeon |date=January 3, 2012 |title=CR Holiday Interview #14 – Steve Bissette |url=http://www.comicsreporter.com/index.php/cr_holiday_interview_11_steve_bissette/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120108052410/http://www.comicsreporter.com/index.php/cr_holiday_interview_11_steve_bissette/ |archive-date=January 8, 2012 |access-date=December 6, 2013 |work=[[The Comics Reporter]]}}</ref>

In the United Kingdom, [[Titan Magazines]] published comics based on ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' every four weeks from February&nbsp;3, 2005,<ref>{{cite web |date=August 19, 2011 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants Magazine 100th Issue |url=http://titanmagazines.com/news/announcements/spongebob-squarepants-magazine-100th-issue/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111006050305/http://titanmagazines.com/news/announcements/spongebob-squarepants-magazine-100th-issue/ |archive-date=October 6, 2011 |access-date=May 22, 2013 |publisher=[[Titan Magazines]]}}</ref> through November&nbsp;28, 2013.<ref>{{Cite web |title=SpongeBob SquarePants Magazine @ Titan Magazines |url=https://titanmagazines.com/t/spongebob-squarepants/?locale=uk |website=titanmagazines.com}}</ref> Titan Magazines also teamed up with [[Lego]] to release a limited edition ''SpongeBob''-themed comic.<ref>{{cite web |last=Hutchins |first=Rob |date=March 22, 2013 |title=SpongeBob LEGO limited edition magazine launches |url=http://www.licensing.biz/news/10992/SpongeBob-Magazine-unites-with-LEGO |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170707123937/http://www.licensing.biz/news/read/spongebob-lego-limited-edition-magazine-launches/027694 |archive-date=July 7, 2017 |access-date=May 22, 2013 |publisher=Licensing}}</ref>

===Films===
{{Main|SpongeBob SquarePants (film series)|l1 = ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' (film series)}}

Six ''SpongeBob'' films have been released theatrically or via streaming services: ''The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie'' (2004), ''The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge Out of Water'' (2015), ''The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge on the Run'' (2020), ''[[Saving Bikini Bottom: The Sandy Cheeks Movie]]'' (2024), and ''[[Plankton: The Movie]]'' (2025), and ''[[The SpongeBob Movie: Search for SquarePants]]'' (2025).<ref>{{cite web |author=Anthony D'Alessandro |date=February 15, 2022 |title=''SpongeBob'' Universe Expands With Three Paramount+ Spinoff Movies, New Theatrical Film |url=https://deadline.com/2022/02/spongebob-squarepants-paramount-plus-movies-theatrical-1234933589/ |access-date=February 15, 2022 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> The series' regular voice actors have reprised their roles for each film. 

====Main series====
The first ''SpongeBob'' film, ''The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie'', an animated film [[adaptation]] of the series, was released on November&nbsp;19, 2004.<ref>{{cite web |title=SpongeBob SquarePants: The Movie (2004) - Financial Information |url=https://www.the-numbers.com/movie/SpongeBob-SquarePants-The-Movie |access-date=July 3, 2026 |website=[[The Numbers (website)|The Numbers]]}}</ref> The film was directed by Hillenburg and written by long-time series writers Derek Drymon, Tim Hill, [[Kent Osborne]], [[Aaron Springer]], Paul Tibbitt, and Hillenburg. He and Julia Pistor produced the film, while Gregor Narholz composed the [[film score|film's score]].<ref>{{cite web |date=March 9, 2005 |title=APM Film and Television Composer Gregor Narholz Signs on to Score Activision's X-Men(TM) Legends Sequel |url=http://investor.activision.com/releasedetail.cfm?ReleaseID=157576 |access-date=August 18, 2013 |publisher=[[Activision]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=March 10, 2005 |title=Gregor Narholz Scores X-Men |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2005/03/10/gregor-narholz-scores-x-men |access-date=August 18, 2013 |website=[[IGN]]}}</ref> Its plot concerns Plankton's evil plan to steal King Neptune's crown and send it to Shell City. SpongeBob and Patrick must retrieve it and save Mr. Krabs' life from Neptune's raft and their home, Bikini Bottom, from Plankton's plan. It features guest appearances by [[Jeffrey Tambor]] as King Neptune, [[Scarlett Johansson]] as the King's daughter Mindy, [[Alec Baldwin]] as Dennis, and [[David Hasselhoff]] as himself.<ref name="Johansson">{{cite video |title=The Absorbing Tale Behind The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie. The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie |date=2005 |medium=DVD |publisher=[[Paramount Home Entertainment]] |people=[[Scarlett Johansson|Johansson, Scarlett]]}}</ref> The film received a positive critical reception<ref name="tomatoes">{{cite web |title=The Spongebob Squarepants Movie (2004) |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/spongebob_squarepants_movie/ |access-date=July 9, 2010 |work=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |publisher=[[Flixster]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=SpongeBob SquarePants Movie, The |url=https://www.metacritic.com/video/titles/spongebobsquarepantsmovie |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20050306091923/https://www.metacritic.com/video/titles/spongebobsquarepantsmovie |archive-date=March 6, 2005 |access-date=July 9, 2010 |work=[[Metacritic]] |publisher=[[CBS]]}}</ref> and was a box office success, grossing over $140 million worldwide.<ref name="BOM">{{cite web |title=The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie (2004) |url=https://boxofficemojo.com/movies/?id=spongebob.htm |access-date=July 20, 2009 |website=[[Box Office Mojo]]}}</ref>

A sequel to the 2004 film, ''The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge Out of Water'', was released in theaters on February&nbsp;6, 2015.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Sneider |first1=Jeff |date=June 5, 2014 |title=Paramount Avoids ''Fifty Shades'' by Moving Up ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' Sequel |url=https://www.thewrap.com/paramount-avoids-fifty-shades-by-moving-up-spongebob-squarepants-sequel/ |access-date=June 7, 2014 |website=[[The Wrap]]}}</ref> The series' main cast members reprised their roles.<ref name="WN">{{cite web |date=March 4, 2013 |title='SpongeBob SquarePants' Film Planned for 2014 |url=http://article.wn.com/view/2012/03/04/SpongeBob_SquarePants_Film_Planned_for_2014/#/related_news |access-date=March 8, 2013 |publisher=WN.com}}</ref> The underwater parts are [[animated traditionally]] in the manner of the series—the live-action parts use [[CGI animation]] for the SpongeBob characters.<ref>{{cite web |last=Webb |first=Charles |date=August 20, 2012 |title=Is Paramount Prepping an Animated 'Legend of Korra' Movie? |url=http://geek-news.mtv.com/2012/08/20/legend-of-korra-movie |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130512062513/http://geek-news.mtv.com/2012/08/20/legend-of-korra-movie |archive-date=May 12, 2013 |access-date=March 8, 2013 |publisher=[[MTV]]}}</ref><ref name="Tradition">{{cite web |last=Desowitz |first=Bill |date=February 29, 2012 |title=SpongeBob kicks off new Paramount Ani division |url=http://billdesowitz.com/spongebob-kicks-off-new-paramount-ani-division/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131022015510/http://billdesowitz.com/spongebob-kicks-off-new-paramount-ani-division/ |archive-date=October 22, 2013 |access-date=March 31, 2013 |publisher=Bill Desowitz}}</ref> The film had a budget similar to the previous film, costing less than $100 million to produce.<ref name="Hundred">{{cite news |last=Chozik |first=Amy |date=March 4, 2012 |title=Return to Big Screen for SpongeBob |url=http://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/03/04/return-to-big-screen-for-spongebob/ |access-date=April 25, 2013 |work=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Goodwin |first=Liam |date=February 28, 2012 |title=New SpongeBob SquarePants movie will be released in 2014 |url=http://filmonic.com/spongebob-squarepants-movie-2014-release-date |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120302143834/http://filmonic.com/spongebob-squarepants-movie-2014-release-date |archive-date=March 2, 2012 |access-date=April 25, 2013 |publisher=Filmonic.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Wolfe |first=Jennifer |date=February 29, 2012 |title=Paramount to Release 'SpongeBob' Movie in 2014 |url=http://www.awn.com/news/people/paramount-release-spongebob-movie-2014 |access-date=April 25, 2013 |publisher=[[Animation World Network]]}}</ref> It was met with positive reviews,<ref>{{Cite web |title=The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge Out of Water {{!}} Rotten Tomatoes |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/the_spongebob_movie_sponge_out_of_water |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |language=en}}</ref> and was also a financial success, grossing over $325.2 million worldwide.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge Out of Water |url=https://www.boxofficemojo.com/release/rl158565889/ |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=Box Office Mojo}}</ref>

A third film, ''The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge on the Run'', was initially scheduled for a May 2020 release. However, due to the COVID-19 pandemic, the film faced multiple delays.<ref>{{cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=April 2, 2020 |title=''Top Gun Maverick'' Flies To Christmas Corridor, ''SpongeBob'' Eyes Late Summer, ''Quiet Place II'' To Debut Labor Day |url=https://deadline.com/2020/04/top-gun-maverick-flies-to-christmas-corridor-spongebob-eyes-late-summer-quiet-place-ii-to-debut-labor-day-1202898738/ |access-date=April 2, 2020 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> In June 2020, its worldwide theatrical release was canceled, prompting Paramount to release the film as a launch-day exclusive for its [[premium video on demand]] and streaming service Paramount+ in the US on March 4, 2021.<ref>{{cite web |last=Rubin |first=Rebecca |date=June 22, 2020 |title=''SpongeBob Movie: Sponge on the Run'' Skipping Theaters to Launch On Demand and CBS All Access (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2020/film/news/spongebob-movie-skipping-theaters-cbs-all-access-1203539493/ |access-date=June 23, 2020 |work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> Internationally, Canada received a theatrical release on August 14, 2020,<ref>{{cite tweet |number=1288988083514482688 |user=ParamountCanada |title=The happiest place on earth is a pineapple under the sea! Paramount Pictures Canada is excited to announce that THE #SPONGEBOBMOVIE: SPONGE ON THE RUN will open exclusively in Canadian theatres on August 14th. |author=Paramount Canada |date=July 30, 2020 |access-date=July 30, 2020}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Amidi |first=Amid |author-link=Amid Amidi |date=July 31, 2020 |title='Sponge on the Run' Will Open Theatrically – But Only in Canada |url=https://www.cartoonbrew.com/feature-film/sponge-on-the-run-will-open-theatrically-but-only-in-canada-195019.html |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=Cartoon Brew |language=en-US}}</ref> while Netflix acquired the streaming rights in foreign regions excluding the US, China, and Canada on November 5, 2020.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=d'Alessandro |first1=Anthony |date=July 17, 2020 |title=Viacom Unloads Foreign Rights For 'SpongeBob: Sponge On The Run' To Netflix – Deadline |url=https://deadline.com/2020/07/spongebob-sponge-on-the-run-foreign-rights-sold-to-netflix-1202986875/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200717082607/https://deadline.com/2020/07/spongebob-sponge-on-the-run-foreign-rights-sold-to-netflix-1202986875/ |archive-date=July 17, 2020 |access-date=March 10, 2025 |work=Deadline}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=West |first=Amy |date=October 26, 2020 |title=New SpongeBob movie that skipped cinemas is coming to Netflix in November |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/movies/a34484315/spongebob-sponge-on-the-run-netflix-premiere-date/ |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=Digital Spy |language=en-GB}}</ref> Unlike the previous two films, this installment primarily uses stylized CGI animation. The film received mixed-to-positive reviews from critics, though audience reception was less favorable.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge on the Run {{!}} Rotten Tomatoes |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/the_spongebob_movie_sponge_on_the_run |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |language=en}}</ref> The film grossed $4.8 million from its limited theatrical runs.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge on the Run |url=https://www.boxofficemojo.com/release/rl2558297601/ |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=Box Office Mojo}}</ref>

''The SpongeBob Movie: Search for SquarePants'' had a world premiere at the AFI Film Festival on October 26, 2025. Its theatrical release was initially set for May&nbsp;23, 2025,<ref>{{cite web |author=Brian Welk |date=April 27, 2023 |title=Paramount Gets Animated with CinemaCon Presentation |url=https://www.indiewire.com/2023/04/spongebob-squarepants-4-transformers-one-animated-cast-1234833032/ |access-date=April 28, 2023 |work=[[IndieWire]]}}</ref> but was delayed until December&nbsp;19.<ref name="DeadlineStrikeDelay">{{cite news |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=October 23, 2023 |title=''Mission: Impossible 8'' Jumps To 2025; ''A Quiet Place: Day One'' Goes To Summer In 2024 Theatrical Shake-Up Due To Actors Strike |url=https://deadline.com/2023/10/mission-impossible-dead-reckoning-part-2-quiet-place-day-one-actors-strike-1235580981/ |access-date=July 6, 2026 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> It is the fourth main ''SpongeBob'' film as well as the franchise's sixth film overall.<ref>{{cite web |title=The SpongeBob Movie: Search for SquarePants |url=https://www.the-numbers.com/movie/SpongeBob-Movie-Search-for-SquarePants-The-(2025) |access-date=July 6, 2026 |website=[[The Numbers (website)|The Numbers]]}}</ref>

====Spin-off films====
''Saving Bikini Bottom: The Sandy Cheeks Movie'' is an animated adventure comedy film released on Netflix on August&nbsp;2, 2024.<ref>{{cite web |author=Carolyn Giardina |date=April 25, 2023 |title=Netflix Animation Reveals ''In Your Dreams'', a New SpongeBob Adventure and Additional ''Nimona'' Voice Casting |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/netflix-animation-in-your-dreams-spongebob-nimona-chicken-run-1235398448/ |access-date=April 28, 2023 |work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> It is the first character-focused spin-off film, as well as the franchise's fourth film overall. It centers around Sandy and SpongeBob going on a mission to save Bikini Bottom, while a subplot centers on the latter's family's exploits in the Circus. Prior to its release, the entire film was leaked on January&nbsp;21, 2024, as a video upload on X (the website formerly known as Twitter).<ref>{{cite web |author=Abdul Azim Naushad |date=January 22, 2024 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants Saving Bikini Bottom: Has the New Sandy Cheeks Movie Leaked? |url=https://www.comingsoon.net/guides/news/1499120-spongebob-squarepants-saving-bikini-bottom-has-the-new-sandy-cheeks-movie-leaked |access-date=January 22, 2024 |work=[[Comingsoon.net]]}}</ref> The film received mixed reviews from critics.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Saving Bikini Bottom: The Sandy Cheeks Movie {{!}} Rotten Tomatoes |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/saving_bikini_bottom_the_sandy_cheeks_movie |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |language=en}}</ref>

''Plankton: The Movie'' is an animated musical comedy film which was released on Netflix on March 7, 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Warner |first=Sam |date=March 7, 2025 |title=A new SpongeBob SquarePants movie has just arrived on Netflix |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/movies/a64083994/spongebob-squarepants-plankton-movie-netflix/ |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=Digital Spy |language=en-GB}}</ref> It is the second character-focused spin-off film, and the fifth film in the franchise overall. As with the ''Sandy Cheeks Movie'', the entire film was leaked onto X (Twitter) in August 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Amidi |first=Amid |author-link=Amid Amidi |date=August 9, 2024 |title=Major Netflix Animation Leak Traced Back To Burbank Post-Production Company |url=https://www.cartoonbrew.com/business/major-netflix-animation-leak-traced-back-to-burbank-post-production-company-242321.html |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=Cartoon Brew |language=en-US}}</ref>

Three [[television films]] were also released: ''SpongeBob's Atlantis SquarePantis'' (2007), ''SpongeBob's Truth or Square'' (2009), and ''SpongeBob's Big Birthday Blowout'' (2019).<ref name="krabby patty kollab" />

===Music===
Collections of original music featured in the series have been released on the albums ''[[SpongeBob SquarePants: Original Theme Highlights]]'' (2001), ''[[SpongeBob's Greatest Hits]]'' (2009), and ''The Yellow Album'' (2005). The first two charted on the US [[Billboard 200|''Billboard'' 200]], reaching number 171 and 122, respectively.<ref>{{cite web |title=SpongeBob SquarePants: Original Theme Highlights |url=https://www.allmusic.com/album/spongebob-squarepants-original-theme-highlights-mw0000012957/awards |access-date=December 7, 2013 |website=[[AllMusic]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=SpongeBob's Greatest Hits |url=https://www.allmusic.com/album/spongebobs-greatest-hits-mw0000810167/awards |access-date=December 7, 2013 |website=AllMusic}}</ref>

Several songs have been recorded for the purpose of a single or album release and have not been featured on the show. The song "My Tighty Whiteys" written by Tom Kenny and [[Andy Paley]] was released only on the album ''[[The Best Day Ever]]'' (2006). Kenny's inspiration for the song was "underwear humor,"<ref name="Newsday">{{cite web |last=Bubbeo |first=Daniel |date=November 5, 2006 |title=FAST CHAT TOM KENNY |url=http://www.newsday.com/entertainment/ny-fffast4956134nov05,0,4012699.story?coll=ny-entertainment-promo |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080217024149/http://www.newsday.com/entertainment/ny-fffast4956134nov05%2C0%2C4012699.story?coll=ny-entertainment-promo |archive-date=February 17, 2008 |access-date=August 2, 2013 |work=Newsday}}</ref> saying: "Underwear humor is always a surefire laugh-getter with kids ... Just seeing a character that odd wearing really prosaic, normal, [[Kmart (United States)|Kmart]], three-to-a-pack underwear is a funny drawing ... We thought it was funny to make a really lush, beautiful love song to his underwear."<ref name="Newsday" />

A soundtrack album, ''The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie – Music from the Movie and More'', featuring the film's score, was released along with the feature-length film in November 2004. Various artists including [[the Flaming Lips]],<ref name="TFL1">{{cite magazine |title=Lips, Shins Kick Back With 'SpongeBob' |url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/65812/lips-shins-kick-back-with-spongebob |access-date=August 18, 2013 |magazine=Billboard}}</ref> [[Wilco]],<ref name="WilcoLips">{{cite web |date=October 13, 2004 |title=Flaming Lips and Wilco Featured on New SpongeBob Soundtrack |url=https://www.pastemagazine.com/articles/2004/10/flaming-lips-and-wilco-featured-on-new-spongebob-s.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091226234145/https://www.pastemagazine.com/articles/2004/10/flaming-lips-and-wilco-featured-on-new-spongebob-s.html |archive-date=December 26, 2009 |access-date=August 18, 2013 |work=Paste}}</ref> Ween,<ref name="MTV">{{cite web |last=Stock |first=Rosina |date=June 24, 2009 |title=Nickelodeon Celebrates Pop Culture Icon ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' decade |url=http://mnilive.com/2009/06/nickelodeon-celebrates-pop-culture-icon-spongebob-squarepants-decade/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090626060310/http://mnilive.com/2009/06/nickelodeon-celebrates-pop-culture-icon-spongebob-squarepants-decade/ |archive-date=June 26, 2009 |access-date=July 14, 2009 |work=Media News International}}</ref> [[Motörhead]],<ref name="MTV2">{{cite web |last=D'Angelo |first=Joe |title=Flaming Lips, Wilco, 'Commercial Weirdo' Avril Lavigne Head Up 'SpongeBob' LP |url=http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1491510/avril-lavigne-flaming-lips-on-spongebob-lp.jhtml |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111025195508/http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1491510/avril-lavigne-flaming-lips-on-spongebob-lp.jhtml |archive-date=October 25, 2011 |access-date=August 18, 2013 |publisher=MTV}}</ref> [[the Shins]],<ref name="Wierdo">{{cite web |last=Dufour |first=Matt |title=SpongeBob Soundtrack Boasts Shins, Wilco, And Flaming Lips Songs |url=http://www.thefader.com/2004/10/04/spongebob-soundtrack-boasts-shins-wilco-and-flaming-lips-songs/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131207145020/http://www.thefader.com/2004/10/04/spongebob-soundtrack-boasts-shins-wilco-and-flaming-lips-songs/ |archive-date=December 7, 2013 |access-date=August 18, 2013 |work=The Fader}}</ref> and Avril Lavigne<ref name="Bands" /> contributed to the soundtrack that reached number 76 on the US ''Billboard'' 200.<ref>{{cite web |title=The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie: Music From the Movie and More |url=https://www.allmusic.com/album/the-spongebob-squarepants-movie-music-from-the-movie-and-more-mw0000674021/awards |access-date=December 7, 2013 |website=[[AllMusic]]}}</ref>

===Theme park rides===
[[File:EF-Mall of America.jpg|thumb|alt=Photograph of the entrance and lift hill of the SpongeBob SquarePants Rock Bottom Plunge ride at the Mall of America. | Entrance and lift hill of the [[SpongeBob SquarePants Rock Bottom Plunge]] ride at the [[Mall of America]]]]
A [[SpongeBob SquarePants 4-D]] film and ride opened at several locations, including [[Six Flags Over Texas]], [[Flamingo Land Resort]], and the [[Shedd Aquarium]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Chicago &#124; Plan a Visit &#124; Now Playing in 4-D |url=http://www.sheddaquarium.org/4dtheater.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101129122646/http://sheddaquarium.org/4dtheater.html |archive-date=November 29, 2010 |access-date=September 14, 2010 |publisher=[[Shedd Aquarium]]}}</ref> The ride features water squirts, real bubbles, and other sensory features. In 2012, Nickelodeon teamed up again with SimEx-Iwerks Entertainment and Super 78 to produce ''SpongeBob SquarePants 4-D: The Great Jelly Rescue''.<ref>{{cite web |last=Arrant |first=Chris |date=September 25, 2012 |title="SpongeBob SquarePants" 4-D Attraction Coming Soon |url=http://www.cartoonbrew.com/biz/spongebob-squarepants-4-d-attraction-coming-soon-70391.html |access-date=May 21, 2013}}</ref> The attraction opened in early 2013 at the [[Mystic Aquarium & Institute for Exploration]].<ref name="4DPlot">{{cite web |date=May 17, 2013 |title=SpongeBob goes 4-D at the aquarium |url=http://www.thewesterlysun.com/mysticriverpress/news/spongebob-goes--d-at-the-aquarium/article_3705ab20-bce3-11e2-8678-0019bb2963f4.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131211231455/http://www.thewesterlysun.com/mysticriverpress/news/spongebob-goes--d-at-the-aquarium/article_3705ab20-bce3-11e2-8678-0019bb2963f4.html |archive-date=December 11, 2013 |access-date=May 21, 2013 |publisher=Mystic River Press}}</ref> It was also installed at the [[Nickelodeon Suites Resort Orlando]] in [[Orlando, Florida]].<ref>{{cite web |title=SpongeBob SquarePants 4-D: The Great Jelly Rescue |url=http://eyeonorlando.com/2013/04/spongebob-squarepants-4-d-the-great-jelly-rescue-2/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130503111622/http://eyeonorlando.com/2013/04/spongebob-squarepants-4-d-the-great-jelly-rescue-2/ |archive-date=May 3, 2013 |access-date=May 21, 2013 |work=Eye on Orlando}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Roseboom |first=Matt |title=Nick Hotel debuts new SpongeBob 4D movie and Bikini Bottom character breakfast |url=http://attractionsmagazine.com/blog/2013/04/22/nick-hotel-debuts-new-spongebob-4d-movie-and-bikini-bottom-character-breakfast/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130423114753/http://attractionsmagazine.com/blog/2013/04/22/nick-hotel-debuts-new-spongebob-4d-movie-and-bikini-bottom-character-breakfast/ |archive-date=April 23, 2013 |access-date=May 21, 2013 |work=[[Orlando Attractions Magazine]]}}</ref> The seven-minute film follows SpongeBob, Patrick, and Sandy rescuing the jellyfish of Jellyfish Fields from Plankton's evil clutches.<ref name="4DPlot" /> On May&nbsp;23, 2015, an interactive 3D show titled ''SpongeBob SubPants Adventure'' opened in Texas at [[Moody Gardens]].<ref>{{cite web |date=March 5, 2015 |title=Moody Gardens launches "first of its kind" immersive SpongeBob SubPants Adventure |url=https://blooloop.com/theme-park/news/moody-gardens-launches-first-of-its-kind-immersive-spongebob-subpants-adventure/ |access-date=July 4, 2026 |website=Blooloop}}</ref> The show was replaced with a generic "20,000 Leagues Under the Sea" re-theme in 2019.<ref>{{Cite web |title=MOODY GARDENS NEWEST INTERACTIVE ADVENTURE GOES 20,000 LEAGUES UNDER THE SEA – Moody Gardens |url=http://blog.moodygardens.com/moody-gardens-newest-interactive-adventure-goes-20000-leagues-under-the-sea/ |access-date=November 27, 2022 |language=en-US}}</ref> A [[dark ride]] shooter attraction titled ''[[SpongeBob's Crazy Carnival Ride]]'' opened at the Circus Circus Resort in [[Las Vegas, Nevada]] in 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |date=November 15, 2023 |title=Sally Dark Rides unveils animatronic at IAAPA Expo in Orlando for SpongeBob's Crazy Carnival Ride |url=https://www.gottagoorlando.com/post/sally-dark-rides-unveils-animatronic-at-iaapa-expo-in-orlando-for-spongebob-s-crazy-carnival-ride |access-date=November 15, 2023 |website=www.gottagoorlando.com}}</ref>

A variety of ''SpongeBob SquarePants''-related attractions are currently located within [[Nickelodeon in amusement parks|Nickelodeon themed-areas]] at [[Movie Park Germany]], [[Pleasure Beach Blackpool]], [[Sea World (Australia)|Sea World]], [[American Dream Meadowlands]], and [[Mall of America]], which includes the [[SpongeBob SquarePants Rock Bottom Plunge]] [[Gerstlauer Euro-Fighter|euro-fighter]] [[roller coaster]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Weeks III |first=John A. |title=Mall Of America Roller Coasters |url=https://www.johnweeks.com/tour/moa/index.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120401050728/https://www.johnweeks.com/tour/moa/index.html |archive-date=2012-04-01 |access-date=2026-09-21 |website=www.johnweeks.com}}</ref>

In 2026, the [[Universal Kids Resort]] in [[Frisco, Texas|Frisco]], [[Texas]] opened "Nickelodeon's SpongeBob SquarePants Bikini Bottom", a themed area with four rides.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Taylor |first=Blake |date=2026-05-28 |title=Universal's first 'SpongeBob Squarepants' land |url=https://attractionsmagazine.com/spongebob-squarepants-bikini-bottom-land-universal-kids-theme-park-rides/ |access-date=2026-09-07 |website=Attractions Magazine |language=en-US}}</ref>

===Video games===
{{main|SpongeBob SquarePants video games|l1 = ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' video games}}

Numerous [[video game]]s based on the series have been produced. Some of the early games include: ''[[SpongeBob SquarePants: Legend of the Lost Spatula|Legend of the Lost Spatula]]'' (2001)<ref>{{cite web |last=Provo |first=Frank |date=March 19, 2001 |title=SpongeBob Squarepants Review |url=https://www.gamespot.com/reviews/spongebob-squarepants-review/1900-2697223/ |access-date=July 3, 2026 |website=[[GameSpot]]}}</ref> and ''[[SpongeBob SquarePants: Battle for Bikini Bottom]]'' (2003). In 2013, Nickelodeon published and distributed ''[[SpongeBob Moves In!]]'', a [[freemium]] [[city-building game]] [[Application software|app]] developed by [[Kung Fu Factory]] for [[iOS]] and [[Android (operating system)|Android]].<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Stecker |first=Erin |date=June 5, 2013 |title='SpongeBob SquarePants' debuts new app – EXCLUSIVE VIDEO |url=http://family-room.ew.com/2013/06/05/spongebob-squarepants-spongebob-moves-in-app/ |access-date=July 13, 2013 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Milligan |first=Mercedes |date=June 6, 2013 |title=Nick Launches Building 'SpongeBob' App |url=http://www.animationmagazine.net/gaming/nick-launches-city-building-spongebob-app/ |access-date=July 13, 2013 |work=[[Animation Magazine|Animation]]}}</ref> On June&nbsp;5, 2019, THQ Nordic announced ''[[SpongeBob SquarePants: Battle for Bikini Bottom – Rehydrated]]'', a full remake of the console versions of the original 2003 game.<ref>{{cite web |last=Lanier |first=Liz |date=June 5, 2019 |title=Classic Spongebob Squarepants Game Getting Remake, Multiplayer Mode |url=https://variety.com/2019/gaming/news/spongebob-rehydrated-announce-1203233815/ |access-date=April 20, 2020 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref><ref name="Destruct">{{cite web |last=Moyce |first=Chris |date=June 5, 2019 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants: Battle for Bikini Bottom getting remastered for PC and consoles |url=https://www.destructoid.com/spongebob-squarepants-battle-for-bikini-bottom-getting-remastered-for-pc-and-consoles-556026.phtml |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200806200006/https://www.destructoid.com/spongebob-squarepants-battle-for-bikini-bottom-getting-remastered-for-pc-and-consoles-556026.phtml |archive-date=August 6, 2020 |access-date=June 5, 2019 |website=[[Destructoid]]}}</ref><ref name="Push">{{cite web |last=Tailby |first=Stephen |date=June 5, 2019 |title=Are You Ready, Kids? SpongeBob SquarePants: Battle for Bikini Bottom – Rehydrated Announced |url=http://www.pushsquare.com/news/2019/06/are_you_ready_kids_spongebob_squarepants_battle_for_bikini_bottom_-_rehydrated_announced |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190605143730/http://www.pushsquare.com/news/2019/06/are_you_ready_kids_spongebob_squarepants_battle_for_bikini_bottom_-_rehydrated_announced |archive-date=June 5, 2019 |access-date=June 5, 2019 |website=[[Push Square]]}}</ref> The game was released one year later on June&nbsp;23, 2020<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bailey |first=Dustin |date=April 16, 2020 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants: Battle for Bikini Bottom hits Steam in June |url=https://www.pcgamesn.com/spongebob-squarepants-battle-for-bikini-bottom-rehydrated/steam-release-date |access-date=April 21, 2020 |website=PCGamesN |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Romano |first=Sal |date=April 16, 2020 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants: Battle for Bikini Bottom – Rehydrated launches June 23 |url=https://www.gematsu.com/2020/04/spongebob-squarepants-battle-for-bikini-bottom-rehydrated-launches-june-23 |access-date=April 16, 2020 |website=Gematsu}}</ref> and includes cut content from the original game.<ref>{{cite web |title=SpongeBob SquarePants: Battle For Bikini Bottom – Rehydrated Release Date Announced |url=https://www.gamespot.com/articles/spongebob-squarepants-battle-for-bikini-bottom-reh/1100-6476124/ |access-date=April 19, 2020}}</ref> On May&nbsp;28, 2020, [[Apple Arcade]] released a game called ''SpongeBob SquarePants: Patty Pursuit''.<ref>{{cite web |last=Brown |first=Shelby |date=May 28, 2020 |title=SpongeBob: Patty Pursuit is the ultimate new Apple Arcade game for fans |url=https://www.cnet.com/news/spongebob-patty-pursuit-is-the-ultimate-new-apple-arcade-game-for-fans/ |access-date=May 13, 2021 |work=[[CNET]]}}</ref> in 2021, [[EA Sports]] introduced a SpongeBob-themed level to the Yard section of its ''[[Madden NFL 21]]'' video game.<ref>{{cite web |last=Peters |first=Jay |date=January 8, 2021 |title=Madden 21 now has a SpongeBob SquarePants field |url=https://www.theverge.com/2021/1/8/22220669/madden-spongebob-squarepants-field-reef-top-the-yard |access-date=January 9, 2021 |work=[[The Verge]]}}</ref>

On September&nbsp;17, 2021, THQ Nordic announced ''[[SpongeBob SquarePants: The Cosmic Shake|SpongeBob Squarepants: The Cosmic Shake]]'', a new original game based on the franchise, which was released on January 31, 2023.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Borthwick |first=Ben |date=September 20, 2021 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants: The Cosmic Shake is an all new 3D platformer coming to consoles and PC |url=https://www.videogamer.com/news/spongebob-squarepants-the-cosmic-shake-is-an-all-new-3d-platformer-coming-to-consoles-and-pc/ |access-date=January 6, 2022 |website=VideoGamer.com |language=en-US}}</ref> It was followed by a sequel, ''[[SpongeBob SquarePants: Titans of the Tide]]'', released on November 18, 2025.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Hesse |first1=Brendan |last2=Bitner |first2=Jon |date=6 August 2025 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants: Titans of the Tide Preorders Include Cheeky Bonus Costumes |url=https://www.gamespot.com/articles/spongebob-squarepants-titans-of-the-tide-preorder-guide/1100-6533664 |access-date=17 August 2025 |website=[[GameSpot]]}}</ref>

===SpongeBob SquareShorts===
Nickelodeon launched the first global ''SpongeBob SquarePants''-themed [[film|short film]] competition, '''SpongeBob SquareShorts: Original Fan Tributes''', in 2013.<ref>{{cite news |last=Wolfe |first=Jennifer |date=January 23, 2013 |title=Nick Launches 2013 Short Film Contest |url=http://www.awn.com/news/call-entries/nick-launches-2013-short-film-contest |access-date=May 23, 2013 |newspaper=[[Animation World Magazine]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Milligan |first=Mercedes |date=May 7, 2013 |title=Nick Launches SpongeBob SquareShorts Contest |url=http://www.animationmagazine.net/events/nick-launches-spongebob-squareshorts-contest/ |access-date=May 23, 2013 |work=Animation}}</ref> The contest encouraged fans and filmmakers around the world to create original short films inspired by SpongeBob for a chance to win a prize and a trip for four people to a screening event in [[Hollywood, Los Angeles|Hollywood]]. The contest opened on May&nbsp;6 and ran through June&nbsp;28, 2013.<ref>{{cite web |title=SpongeBob Square Shorts Competition – $2,500 + Trip |url=http://www.filmthenext.com/2013/06/spongebob-square-shorts-competition-2500-trip/ |access-date=May 23, 2013 |website=FilmTheNext.com}}</ref><ref name="Contest">{{cite web |last=Kondolojy |first=Amanda |date=May 7, 2013 |title=Nickelodeon Announces First-Ever ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' Global Film Competition, 'SpongeBob SquareShorts: Original Fan Tributes' |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2013/05/07/nickelodeon-announces-first-ever-spongebob-squarepants-global-film-competition-spongebob-squareshorts-original-fan-tributes/181318/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130511005553/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2013/05/07/nickelodeon-announces-first-ever-spongebob-squarepants-global-film-competition-spongebob-squareshorts-original-fan-tributes/181318/ |archive-date=May 11, 2013 |access-date=May 23, 2013 |publisher=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref> On July&nbsp;19, 2013, Nickelodeon announced the competition's finalists.<ref>{{cite web |last=Hutchins |first=Rob |date=July 22, 2013 |title=Nickelodeon reveals finalists in SpongeBob Squareshorts film comp |url=http://www.licensing.biz/news/11767/Nickelodeon-reveals-finalists-in-SpongeBob-Squareshorts-film-competition |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131024040444/http://www.licensing.biz/news/read/nickelodeon-reveals-finalists-in-spongebob-squareshorts-film-comp/026966 |archive-date=October 24, 2013 |access-date=July 22, 2013 |publisher=[[Licensing.biz]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=July 19, 2013 |title=Nickelodeon Announces Finalists For First-Ever SpongeBob SquareShorts Global Short Film Competition |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2013/07/19/nickelodeon-announces-finalists-for-first-ever-spongebob-squareshorts-global-short-film-competition-92000/20130719nickelodeon01/ |access-date=July 22, 2013 |work=[[The Futon Critic]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Liu |first=Ed |date=July 19, 2013 |title=PR: Nickelodeon Announces Finalists for First-Ever "SpongeBob SquareShorts: Original Fan Tributes" |url=http://www.toonzone.net/2013/07/nickelodeon-announces-finalists-for-first-ever-spongebob-squareshorts-original-fan-tributes/#.Ue0FftIwe5I |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131218233942/http://www.toonzone.net/2013/07/nickelodeon-announces-finalists-for-first-ever-spongebob-squareshorts-original-fan-tributes/#.Ue0FftIwe5I |archive-date=December 18, 2013 |access-date=July 22, 2013 |work=Toonzone}}</ref> On August&nbsp;13, 2013, the under-18 category was won by David of the United States for his ''The Krabby Commercial'', while the ''Finally Home'' short by Nicole of [[South Africa]] won the 18 and over category.<ref>{{Cite web |date=August 9, 2013 |title=Nickelodeon Announces Winners for First-Ever 'SpongeBob SquarePants' Global Short Film Competition |url=https://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/network-press-releases/nickelodeon-announces-winners-for-first-ever-spongebob-squarepants-global-short-film-competition/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210307212451/https://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/network-press-releases/nickelodeon-announces-winners-for-first-ever-spongebob-squarepants-global-short-film-competition/ |archive-date=March 7, 2021 |access-date=September 8, 2019 |publisher=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>

===Theater===
{{main|SpongeBob SquarePants (musical)|l1 = ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' (musical)}}

''SpongeBob'' was adapted as a [[stage musical]], ''[[SpongeBob SquarePants, The Broadway Musical]]'', by director [[Tina Landau]]. It premiered in Chicago in 2016 and opened on [[Broadway (Manhattan)|Broadway]] at the [[Palace Theatre (Broadway)|Palace Theatre]] on December&nbsp;4, 2017.<ref>{{cite news |last=Deb |first=Sopan |date=November 22, 2017 |title=With a Singing SpongeBob, Nickelodeon Aims for a Broadway Splash – The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2017/11/22/theater/spongebob-squarepants-the-broadway-musical-nickelodeon.html |access-date=January 11, 2018 |work=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref> It received twelve award nominations at the [[72nd Tony Awards]] in 2018.<ref>{{cite web |date=May 1, 2018 |title=2018 Tony Award Nominations: SpongeBob SquarePants and Mean Girls Lead the Pack |url=http://www.playbill.com/article/2018-tony-award-nominations-spongebob-squarepants-and-mean-girls-lead-the-pack |work=[[Playbill]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Chen |first=Wei-Huan |date=February 16, 2018 |title='SpongeBob' musical underscores nautical nonsense of art vs. entertainment |url=https://www.houstonchronicle.com/entertainment/arts-theater/article/Spongebob-musical-underscores-nautical-nonsense-12620152.php |work=[[Houston Chronicle]]}}</ref>

==Merchandise==
{{further|List of SpongeBob SquarePants merchandise|l1=List of ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' merchandise}}
[[File:SpongeBob-SquarePants-characters-toys.jpg|right|thumb|320px|alt=Photograph of a SpongeBob SquarePants figure set on a beach|A set of ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' figures modeled after the main characters]]
By the time the [[SpongeBob SquarePants (franchise)|''SpongeBob'' franchise]] celebrated its 25th anniversary in 2024, it had generated $16 billion in retail sales.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |last=Olson |first=Cathy Applefeld |date=October 18, 2024 |title=At 25, SpongeBob Franchise Continues To Be Money For Nickelodeon |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/cathyolson/2024/10/18/at-25-spongebob-franchise-continues-to-be-money-for-nickelodeon/ |website=Forbes}}</ref> In 2002, SpongeBob dolls sold at a rate of 75,000 per week—faster than the popular [[Tickle Me Elmo]] dolls were selling at the time.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Strauss |first=Gary |date=May 17, 2002 |title=Life's good for SpongeBob |url=https://www.usatoday.com/money/covers/2002-05-17-spongebob.htm |archive-url=http://usatoday30.usatoday.com/money/covers/2002-05-17-sponge-bob.htm |archive-date=May 21, 2013 |access-date=November 8, 2008 |work=[[USA Today]]}}</ref> By 2007, ''SpongeBob'' merchandise was gaining popularity in Japan, thanks to a carefully orchestrated marketing campaign targeting young women.<ref name="SFGate">{{cite news |last=Kageyama |first=Yuri |date=January 24, 2007 |title=SpongeBob Goes Trendy to Win Japan Fans |url=http://www.sfgate.com/cgi-bin/article.cgi?f=/n/a/2007/01/24/entertainment/e091755S47.DTL |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090405192838/http://www.sfgate.com/cgi-bin/article.cgi?f=%2Fn%2Fa%2F2007%2F01%2F24%2Fentertainment%2Fe091755S47.DTL |archive-date=April 5, 2009 |access-date=November 8, 2008 |work=[[The San Francisco Chronicle]]}}</ref> Popular board games such as ''[[Monopoly (game)|Monopoly]]'',<ref>{{cite web |last=Meehan |first=Alex |date=December 1, 2020 |title=Monopoly: SpongeBob SquarePants Meme Edition lets you buy Mocking SpongeBob and Handsome Squidward |url=https://www.dicebreaker.com/categories/board-game/news/monopoly-spongebob-squarepants-meme-edition-announced |access-date=July 3, 2026 |website=[[Dicebreaker]]}}</ref> ''[[The Game of Life|Life]]'',<ref>{{cite web |last=Onyett |first=Charles |date=September 10, 2008 |title=The Game of Life -SpongeBob SquarePants Edition Review |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2008/09/10/the-game-of-life-spongebob-squarepants-edition-review |access-date=May 22, 2013 |website=[[IGN]]}}</ref> ''[[Operation (game)|Operation]]'',<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Ward |first=Kate |date=November 28, 2009 |title=Hasbro lets us operate on SpongeBob. Which TV character would you like to get inside? |url=http://popwatch.ew.com/2009/11/28/operation-spongebob-tv-characters/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091204035456/http://popwatch.ew.com/2009/11/28/operation-spongebob-tv-characters/ |archive-date=December 4, 2009 |access-date=May 23, 2013 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> ''[[Ants in the Pants (game)|Ants in the Pants]]'',<ref>{{cite web |title=ANTS IN THE SquarePants |url=http://www.hasbro.com/shop/details.cfm?R=927727BC-6D40-1014-8BF0-9EFBF894F9D4:en_US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120622093031/http://www.hasbro.com/shop/details.cfm?R=927727BC-6D40-1014-8BF0-9EFBF894F9D4:en_US |archive-date=June 22, 2012 |access-date=May 23, 2013 |publisher=[[Hasbro]]}}</ref> and ''[[Yahtzee]]'' have been given ''SpongeBob''-themed editions.<ref>{{cite web |title=YAHTZEE Jr. ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' Edition Card Game |url=http://www.hasbro.com/games/en_US/shop/details.cfm?R=8F8A0CA2-5056-900B-1002-5FC898DDBE91:en_US |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120620001213/http://www.hasbro.com/games/en_US/shop/details.cfm?R=8F8A0CA2-5056-900B-1002-5FC898DDBE91:en_US |archive-date=June 20, 2012 |access-date=May 23, 2013 |publisher=[[Hasbro]]}}</ref> SpongeBob toys have been included with children's meals at fast food restaurants around the world.<ref>{{cite web |date=May 17, 2007 |title=Spongebob con l'Happy Meal McDonald's |url=http://www.megamodo.com/200711368-spongebob-con-lhappy-meal-mcdonalds/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140109234852/http://www.megamodo.com/200711368-spongebob-con-lhappy-meal-mcdonalds/ |archive-date=January 9, 2014 |access-date=January 10, 2014 |work=Megamodo |language=it}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Stark |first=Jill |date=October 5, 2007 |title=Maccas takes out 'pester power' prize |url=http://www.theage.com.au/news/national/maccas-takes-out-pester-power-prize/2007/10/04/1191091281190.html |access-date=May 23, 2013 |work=[[The Age]] |location=Melbourne}}</ref> SpongeBob-themed snacks,<ref>{{cite web |date=April 30, 2013 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants Pirates Booty $1 at Target |url=http://www.totallytarget.com/2012/04/30/spongebob-squarepants-pirates-booty-1-at-target/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120501235155/http://www.totallytarget.com/2012/04/30/spongebob-squarepants-pirates-booty-1-at-target/ |archive-date=May 1, 2012 |access-date=May 24, 2013 |publisher=Totally Target}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=March 22, 2013 |title=SpongeBob SplashPants Sweepstakes 5/31/13 1PPD4-14 |url=http://sweetiessweeps.com/2013/03/spongebob-splashpants-sweepstakes.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130327205612/http://sweetiessweeps.com/2013/03/spongebob-splashpants-sweepstakes.html |archive-date=March 27, 2013 |access-date=May 24, 2013 |publisher=Sweetis Sweeps}}</ref> drinks,<ref>{{cite web |last=Meitner |first=Sarah Hale |date=March 2, 2005 |title=Slurpee Galaxy Expands With Nod To 'Star Wars' |url=https://www.orlandosentinel.com/2005/03/02/slurpee-galaxy-expands-with-nod-to-star-wars/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130524054843/http://articles.orlandosentinel.com/2005-03-02/news/0503020192_1_darth-vader-7-eleven-new-flavors |archive-date=May 24, 2013 |access-date=May 22, 2013 |work=[[Orlando Sentinel]]}}</ref> bottled water<ref>{{cite web |last=Weston |first=Shaun |date=June 3, 2013 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants Spring Water |url=http://www.foodbev.com/news/spongebob-squarepants-spring-water#.UbcBF-cwe5I |access-date=June 11, 2013 |work=Food Bev}}</ref> and ice cream have been produced.<ref>{{cite web |last=Weston |first=Shaun |date=May 22, 2013 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants Vanilla Ice Cream |url=http://www.foodbev.com/news/spongebob-squarepants-vanilla-ice-cream#.UbcBjOcwe5J |access-date=June 11, 2013 |work=Food Bev}}</ref> As part of an initiative to encourage children to eat vegetables, SpongeBob was featured on cans of [[Green Giant]] food products.<ref>{{cite web |date=May 31, 2007 |title=Nickelodeon Expands Healthy Food Initiative with Green Giant |url=http://promomagazine.com/entertainmentmarketing/news/nickelodeon_healthy_food_initiative_green_giant_053107/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101230024017/http://promomagazine.com/entertainmentmarketing/news/nickelodeon_healthy_food_initiative_green_giant_053107/ |archive-date=December 30, 2010 |access-date=September 14, 2010 |work=Promomagazine.com}}</ref>

[[Imation]] Electronics Products released ''SpongeBob''-themed electronics,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Veneziani |first1=Vince |date=September 27, 2007 |title=Nickelodeon's NPower Lineup Of Electronics |url=https://techcrunch.com/2007/09/27/nickelodeons-npower-lineup-of-electronics/ |access-date=June 28, 2014 |work=[[TechCrunch]]}}</ref> [[Build-A-Bear Workshop]] produced a ''SpongeBob'' collection,{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{cite web |last=Dedman |first=Christie |date=April 4, 2013 |title=Build A Bear ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' coming May 17 |url=http://blog.al.com/bargain-mom/2013/04/build_a_bear_spongebob_square.html |access-date=May 24, 2013 |publisher=AL.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=May 15, 2013 |title=Build-A-Bear Workshop Makes a Splash with New ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' Collection |url=http://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20130515005084/en/Build-A-Bear-Workshop-Splash-SpongeBob-SquarePants-Collection |access-date=May 24, 2013 |publisher=[[Business Wire]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=May 15, 2013 |title=Build-A-Bear welcomes the SpongeBob gang |url=http://www.retailingtoday.com/article/build-bear-welcomes-spongebob-gang |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130918153644/http://www.retailingtoday.com/article/build-bear-welcomes-spongebob-gang |archive-date=September 18, 2013 |access-date=May 24, 2013 |work=Retailing Today}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Edel |first=Ray |date=May 15, 2013 |title=Make a splash with new ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' Collection at Build-A-Bear |url=http://blog.northjersey.com/thebeat/4415/make-a-splash-with-new-spongebob-squarepants-collection-at-build-a-bear/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131001122705/http://blog.northjersey.com/thebeat/4415/make-a-splash-with-new-spongebob-squarepants-collection-at-build-a-bear/ |archive-date=October 1, 2013 |access-date=May 24, 2013 |publisher=[[NorthJersey.com]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Mierzejewski |first=Ali |date=May 15, 2013 |title=Build-A-Bear Workshop Meets Bikini Bottom with New ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' Collection |url=http://toybook.com/build-a-bear-workshop-meets-bikini-bottom-with-new-spongebob-squarepants-collection/ |access-date=May 24, 2013 |publisher=Toy Book}}</ref>}} and Simmons Jewelry Co. released a $75,000 diamond pendant as part of a ''SpongeBob'' line.<ref name="Pendant" /><ref>{{cite news |date=January 14, 2009 |title=High Fashion Hits Bikini Bottom |url=http://phx.corporate-ir.net/phoenix.zhtml?c=85242&p=irol-newsArticle_pf&ID=1244418&highlight= |access-date=May 23, 2013 |newspaper=Viacom}}</ref> SpongeBob has appeared as a guest character in the video games ''[[Nicktoons Unite!]]'' and ''[[Nicktoons MLB]]'', and in the video game franchise ''[[Nick All-Star Brawl]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Abraham |first=Peter |date=September 7, 2011 |title=Nicktoons MLB video game debuts next week |url=https://www.boston.com/sports/boston-red-sox/2011/09/07/nicktoons_mlb_v/ |access-date=October 31, 2024 |website=www.boston.com |language=en-US}}</ref> SpongeBob [[Skin (video games)|skins]] are available in the mobile games ''Stumble Guys''<ref>{{Cite web |title=Stumble Guys - Patch Notes 0.74 - SpongeBob SquarePants is Back! |url=https://www.stumbleguys.com/news/update74 |access-date=October 31, 2024 |website=Stumble Guys |language=en}}</ref> and ''[[Brawl Stars]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |title=SpongeBob SquarePants shows up in Brawl Stars for a special takeover |url=https://supercell.com/en/news/brawlstars-spongebob/ |access-date=October 31, 2024 |website=Supercell |language=en}}</ref>

In 2013, [[Toyota]] unveiled a ''SpongeBob''-inspired [[Toyota Highlander]] sport utility vehicle on what was dubbed "SpongeBob Day".{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{cite news |last=Ayapana |first=Erick |date=July 15, 2013 |title=Custom Spongebob Squarepants 2014 Toyota Highlander Sets Sail |url=https://www.motortrend.com/news/custom-spongebob-squarepants-2014-toyota-highlander-sets-sail-385945/ |access-date=July 16, 2013 |newspaper=Motortrend |publisher=MotorTrend.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Busis |first=Hillary |date=July 12, 2013 |title=SpongeBob Square...Car? Check out the cartoon's new 'concept vehicle' – EXCLUSIVE |url=http://family-room.ew.com/2013/07/12/spongebob-squarepants-concept-vehicle/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130714103855/http://family-room.ew.com/2013/07/12/spongebob-squarepants-concept-vehicle/ |archive-date=July 14, 2013 |access-date=July 13, 2013 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Brindusescu |first=Gabriel |date=July 12, 2013 |title=Toyota to Unveil 2014 Highlander SpongeBob Edition [Video] |url=http://www.autoevolution.com/toyota-blog/toyota-to-unveil-2014-highlander-spongebob-edition-video-63013.html |access-date=July 13, 2013 |work=Auto Evolution}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Burden |first=Melissa |date=July 12, 2013 |title=Toyota creates one-of-a-kind SpongeBob Highlander |url=http://www.detroitnews.com/article/20130712/AUTO0104/307120114/1361/Toyota-creates-one-of-a-kind-SpongeBob-Highlander |archive-url=https://archive.today/20130713100514/http://www.detroitnews.com/article/20130712/AUTO0104/307120114/1361/Toyota-creates-one-of-a-kind-SpongeBob-Highlander |archive-date=July 13, 2013 |access-date=July 13, 2013 |website=[[The Detroit News]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Barari |first=Arman |date=July 13, 2013 |title=SpongeBob-Themed Toyota Highlander by Nickelodeon |url=http://www.motorward.com/2013/07/spongebob-themed-toyota-highlander-by-nickelodeon/ |access-date=July 13, 2013 |publisher=Motor Ward}}</ref>}} In 2024, Nickelodeon collaborated with the fast food chain [[Wendy's]] to create "Krabby Patty Kollab" meals. The meals included a "Krabby Patty", which was a regular Wendy's burger with a special sauce.<ref name="krabby patty kollab" /> The promotion was criticized by some fans for allegedly going against Hillenburg's wishes of not selling ''SpongeBob''-themed fast food.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Cifarelli |first=David |date=October 11, 2024 |title=Here's why 'SpongeBob Squarepants' fans are upset about Wendy's Krabby Patty |url=https://www.masslive.com/entertainment/2024/10/wendys-krabby-patty-collaboration-sparks-backlash-from-spongebob-fans.html |access-date=October 24, 2024 |website=masslive |language=en}}</ref> In 2019, Nickelodeon released a series of toys inspired by various ''SpongeBob'' Internet memes.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{cite news |last1=Harbison |first1=Cammy Harbison |date=April 24, 2019 |title=A new line of Spongebob Squarepants Masterpiece Memes figurines bring all your favorite SpongeBob memes to life. |url=https://www.newsweek.com/spongebob-meme-toys-nickelodeon-figures-where-buy-mocking-spongebob-toy-1404691 |access-date=April 25, 2019 |work=[[Newsweek]]}}</ref><ref name="p007">{{Cite news |last=Hamilton |first=Xavier |date=April 24, 2019 |title=Nickelodeon Releases Official Spongebob Meme Figures |url=https://www.complex.com/pop-culture/a/fnr-tigg/nickelodeon-releases-official-spongebob-meme-figures |access-date=September 25, 2024 |work=Complex}}</ref><ref name="Romano-2019" />}} The studio has also included references to well-known memes in ''SpongeBob'' video games.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Diaz |first1=Ana |date=September 9, 2021 |title=A SpongeBob SquarePants meme made it into Nickelodeon All-Star Brawl |url=https://www.polygon.com/22665321/meme-spongebob-squarepants-nickelodeon-all-star-brawl-fighting-game |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220831055819/https://www.polygon.com/22665321/meme-spongebob-squarepants-nickelodeon-all-star-brawl-fighting-game |archive-date=August 31, 2022 |access-date=August 31, 2022 |website=Polygon}}</ref>

In 2025, [[Wizards of the Coast]] released a limited edition set of ''SpongeBob-''themed cards for its trading card game ''[[Magic: The Gathering]]'', while the clothing brands [[Uniqlo]] and [[Cactus Plant Flea Market]] collaborated to produce ''SpongeBob-''inspired garments.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{Cite web |last=Fanelli |first=Jason |date=October 25, 2024 |title=Magic: The Gathering's 2025 Lineup Features Final Fantasy, Spider-Man, And SpongeBob |url=https://www.gamespot.com/gallery/magic-the-gatherings-2025-lineup-features-final-fantasy-spider-man-and-spongebob/2900-5889/ |access-date=October 28, 2024 |website=GameSpot |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=December 5, 2024 |title=Uniqlo UT Officially Launches SpongeBob x Cactus Plant Flea Market Collection |url=https://hypebeast.com/2024/12/uniqlo-ut-spongebob-cactus-plant-flea-market-collaboration-release-info |access-date=December 5, 2024 |website=Hypebeast}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=December 5, 2024 |title=Uniqlo UT x CPFM collab page |url=https://www.uniqlo.com/us/en/special-feature/ut/spongebob-cpfm |website=Uniqlo}}</ref>}} The same year, the [[United States Postal Service]] released a series of ''SpongeBob''-themed stamps.{{efn|Attributed to multiple references:<ref>{{Cite web |last=Cross |first=Greta |title=USPS is releasing 'SpongeBob SquarePants' stamps: How to get them |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/money/2025/06/30/usps-spongebob-squarepants-stamps/84416608007/ |access-date=2026-02-09 |website=USA TODAY |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hubbard |first=Amy |date=2025-07-03 |title=SpongeBob and friends are USPS stamps: You can snail-mail any pineapple under the sea |url=https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2025-07-03/spongebob-squarepants-usps-stamp-mail |access-date=2026-02-09 |website=Los Angeles Times |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=''SpongeBob SquarePants'' Iconic Characters To Be Featured on New Forever Stamps |url=https://about.usps.com/newsroom/national-releases/2025/0701ma-spongebob-squarepants-iconic-characters-to-be-featured-on-new-forever-stamps.htm |access-date=2026-02-09 |website=[[United States Postal Service|USPS]] |language=en}}</ref>}}

==Cultural impact==
SpongeBob has become an icon in [[Tahrir Square]] in Cairo, Egypt.<ref name="Egypt Guardian">{{cite news |last=Kingsley |first=Patrick |date=May 27, 2013 |title=How ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' became massive in Egypt |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/shortcuts/2013/may/27/spongebob-squarepants-egypt-cartoon-fame |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200807125447/https://www.theguardian.com/world/shortcuts/2013/may/27/spongebob-squarepants-egypt-cartoon-fame |archive-date=August 7, 2020 |access-date=June 11, 2013 |work=[[The Guardian]] |location=London}}</ref> After the [[Egyptian Revolution of 2011]], the character became a fashion trend, appearing on various garments from [[hijab]]s to [[boxer shorts]].<ref name="Egypt Vice">{{cite web |last=Malsin |first=Jared |date=January 15, 2013 |title=Is ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' the New Che Guevara? |url=https://www.vice.com/en/article/spongebob-squarepants-egypts-new-revolutionary-symbol/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130116151008/https://www.vice.com/read/spongebob-squarepants-egypts-new-revolutionary-symbol |archive-date=January 16, 2013 |access-date=June 11, 2013 |work=[[Vice (magazine)|Vice]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=May 28, 2013 |title=Meet Egypt's unusual Tahrir icon: ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' |url=http://english.alarabiya.net/en/life-style/variety/2013/05/28/Meet-Egypt-s-latest-Tahrir-icon-SpongeBob-SquarePants.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130528173047/http://english.alarabiya.net/en/life-style/variety/2013/05/28/Meet-Egypt-s-latest-Tahrir-icon-SpongeBob-SquarePants.html |archive-date=May 28, 2013 |access-date=June 11, 2013 |work=[[Al Arabiya]]}}</ref> Daniel Kohn of [[Vice (magazine)|''Vice'']] wondered whether SpongeBob had become a symbol of resistance during political turmoil.<ref name="Egypt Vice" /> The Egyptian-American filmmaker Sherief Elkeshta questioned why the images of SpongeBob did not show him holding a [[Molotov cocktail]], or at least raising a fist.<ref>{{cite web |title=Brooklyn, Egypt, And SpongeBob |url=http://www.midanmasr.com/en/article.aspx?ArticleID=208 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130121172006/http://www.midanmasr.com/en/article.aspx?ArticleID=208 |archive-date=January 21, 2013 |access-date=June 11, 2013 |work=Midan Masr}}</ref> The ubiquity of SpongeBob led to the creation of a [[Tumblr]] project called "SpongeBob on the Nile", which was founded by two American students, and which attempts to document every appearance of SpongeBob in Egypt.<ref name="Middle East Prospect">{{cite web |last=Cormack |first=Raphael |date=March 26, 2013 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants takes over the Middle East |url=http://www.prospectmagazine.co.uk/blog/spongebob-squarepants-middle-east-egypt/#.Ubbv5ucwe5I |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130606164927/http://www.prospectmagazine.co.uk/blog/spongebob-squarepants-middle-east-egypt/#.Ubbv5ucwe5I |archive-date=June 6, 2013 |access-date=June 11, 2013 |work=[[Prospect (magazine)|Prospect]]}}</ref> There is also evidence of the phenomenon in [[Libya]], where a rebel in SpongeBob attire was photographed celebrating the revolution.<ref>{{cite web |date=May 28, 2013 |title=The New Mascot of Egypt: ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' |url=http://tavernkeepers.com/the-new-mascot-of-egypt-spongebob-squarepants/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130615083050/http://tavernkeepers.com/the-new-mascot-of-egypt-spongebob-squarepants/ |archive-date=June 15, 2013 |work=Tavern Keepers}}</ref> Although Patrick Kingsley of ''[[The Guardian]]'' stated that the trend has no political significance, facetious presidential campaigns have been launched for SpongeBob in Egypt and Syria.<ref name="Egypt Vice" /><ref name="Middle East Prospect" /><ref name="Egypt Guardian" />

In 2014, a SpongeBob-themed eatery opened in [[Ramallah]], [[West Bank]], [[Palestine]]. The restaurant is modeled after the Krusty Krab and serves Krabby Patties.<ref>{{Cite web |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=June 27, 2014 |title=Spongebob-themed eatery hits Ramallah |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/ramallahs-spongebob-themed-eatery/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190717182227/https://www.timesofisrael.com/ramallahs-spongebob-themed-eatery/ |archive-date=July 17, 2019 |access-date=May 10, 2025 |website=Times of Israel |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=McDonald |first=Soraya Nadia |date=July 22, 2014 |title='SpongeBob's' Krusty Krab is opening — in the West Bank |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/morning-mix/wp/2014/07/22/spongebobs-krusty-krab-is-opening-in-palestine/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140723032630/https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/morning-mix/wp/2014/07/22/spongebobs-krusty-krab-is-opening-in-palestine/ |archive-date=July 23, 2014 |access-date=May 10, 2025 |newspaper=The Washington Post |language=en-US |issn=0190-8286}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=September 11, 2014 |title=Ramallah's own 'Krabby patty' |url=https://www.jpost.com/metro/ramallahs-own-krabby-patty-375066 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250520113325/https://www.jpost.com/metro/ramallahs-own-krabby-patty-375066 |archive-date=May 20, 2025 |access-date=May 10, 2025 |website=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |language=en |issn=0792-822X}}</ref>

Following Hillenburg's death in November 2018, more than 1.2 million fans signed a petition for the [[National Football League]] to have the song "Sweet Victory" from the season 2 episode "[[Band Geeks]]" performed in his honor at the [[Super Bowl LIII]] [[Super Bowl LIII halftime show|halftime show]]. While the song's opening was ultimately included, it served as a transition into the performance of rapper [[Travis Scott]].<ref>{{cite news |author=Baer, Jack |date=February 4, 2019 |title=Where was 'Sweet Victory?' Brief SpongeBob SquarePants appearance at Super Bowl halftime show disappoints |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/sweet-victory-brief-spongebob-squarepants-appearance-super-bowl-halftime-show-disappoints-015346882.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200808201225/https://sports.yahoo.com/amphtml/sweet-victory-brief-spongebob-squarepants-appearance-super-bowl-halftime-show-disappoints-015346882.html |archive-date=August 8, 2020 |access-date=February 5, 2019 |work=[[Yahoo Sports]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Alexander |first=Julia |date=February 3, 2019 |title=Spongebob Squarepants' 'Sweet Victory' finally gets a Super Bowl tribute |url=https://www.theverge.com/2019/2/3/18209868/spongebob-squarepants-sweet-victory-super-bowl-2019-marron-5-halftime-show |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190204012129/https://www.theverge.com/2019/2/3/18209868/spongebob-squarepants-sweet-victory-super-bowl-2019-marron-5-halftime-show |archive-date=February 4, 2019 |access-date=February 3, 2019 |work=[[The Verge]]}}</ref> In response to fans' disappointment at not hearing the complete song, the [[Dallas Stars]] of the [[National Hockey League]] showed a clip of the full song during a game at the [[American Airlines Center]].<ref>{{cite web |date=February 4, 2019 |title=WATCH: Dallas Stars give fans the 'Sweet Victory' SpongeBob halftime show we all deserve |url=https://www.foxsports.com/southwest/story/watch-dallas-stars-give-fans-the-sweet-victory-spongebob-halftime-show-we-all-deserve-020419?amp=true |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190207015252/https://www.foxsports.com/southwest/story/watch-dallas-stars-give-fans-the-sweet-victory-spongebob-halftime-show-we-all-deserve-020419?amp=true |archive-date=February 7, 2019 |access-date=February 5, 2019 |work=[[Fox Sports]]}}</ref> An animated remake of "Sweet Victory" opened Nickelodeon's broadcast of [[Super Bowl LVIII]], implementing clips of the [[2023 San Francisco 49ers season|2023 San Francisco 49ers]] and [[2023 Kansas City Chiefs season|2023 Kansas City Chiefs]] during the performance.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nivison |first=Austin |date=February 11, 2024 |title=Super Bowl 2024: SpongeBob SquarePants will recreate 'Sweet Victory' performance on Nickelodeon before game |url=https://www.cbssports.com/nfl/news/super-bowl-2024-spongebob-squarepants-will-recreate-sweet-victory-performance-on-nickelodeon-before-game/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250317122812/https://www.cbssports.com/nfl/news/super-bowl-2024-spongebob-squarepants-will-recreate-sweet-victory-performance-on-nickelodeon-before-game/ |archive-date=March 17, 2025 |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=CBS Sports |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Moreau |first=Jordan |date=February 12, 2024 |title='SpongeBob' Opens Super Bowl With Rousing 'Sweet Victory' Performance |url=https://variety.com/2024/tv/news/spongebob-super-bowl-sweet-victory-performance-1235902649/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240516033320/https://variety.com/2024/tv/news/spongebob-super-bowl-sweet-victory-performance-1235902649/ |archive-date=May 16, 2024 |access-date=March 10, 2025 |website=Variety |language=en-US}}</ref>

In honor of Hillenburg, a nonprofit fan project titled ''The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie Rehydrated'' was released online on May&nbsp;1, 2022. It consists of a re-creation of ''the SpongeBob SquarePants Movie'', reanimated by 300 people with re-recorded music and dialogue. Amid the YouTube premiere, the video was taken down by [[Paramount Global]] due to copyright laws. As a result, the [[hashtag]] #JusticeForSpongeBob trended on Twitter against Paramount's action. The video was restored the following day.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Jaworski |first=Michelle |date=May 2, 2022 |title='It was a love letter to the franchise and what did Paramount do? They blocked it': Outrage as 'SpongeBob' fan film removed on YouTube |url=https://www.dailydot.com/unclick/spongebob-squarepants-rehydrated/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220503003928/https://www.dailydot.com/unclick/spongebob-squarepants-rehydrated/ |archive-date=May 3, 2022 |access-date=May 7, 2022 |website=[[The Daily Dot]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Coulson |first=Josh |date=May 3, 2022 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants Fan Movie Rehydrated! Goes Live, Gets Copyright Takedown During Premiere |url=https://www.thegamer.com/spongebob-squarepants-rehydrate-copyright-takedown/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220503080136/https://www.thegamer.com/spongebob-squarepants-rehydrate-copyright-takedown/ |archive-date=May 3, 2022 |access-date=May 7, 2022 |website=TheGamer}}</ref>

''SpongeBob'' has been viewed in at least 170 countries and has been available in at least 24 languages.<ref name="New York Daily News" />

===SpongeBob in Internet culture===
[[Internet meme|Online memes]] related to ''SpongeBob'' have achieved widespread popularity on the Internet, with Aja Romano of ''[[Vox (website)|Vox]]'' declaring in 2019 that "Spongebob memes came to rule Internet culture".<ref name="Romano-2019" /> A [[subreddit]] devoted to memes based on the animated series has, as of May 2019, accumulated over 1.7 million subscribers, a figure much higher than subreddits devoted to the series itself.<ref name="Romano-2019" />

Matt Schimkowitz, a senior editor for ''[[Know Your Meme]]'', told ''Time'' magazine that a combination of factors make ''SpongeBob'' memes so popular. He speculated that [[nostalgia]] for the past, alongside the [[cartoon]]'s young audience, contributed to ''SpongeBob SquarePants''' outsized presence in Internet meme culture. Schimkowitz further added that memes derived from the series are exceptionally good at expressing [[emotions]].<ref name="Time">{{cite magazine |last1=Greenspan |first1=Rachel E. |date=September 19, 2019 |title=Your Guide to the Best Spongebob Memes Across the Internet's Sea |url=https://time.com/5647509/best-spongebob-memes/ |access-date=February 24, 2022 |magazine=Time |language=en |archive-date=March 19, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220319085524/https://time.com/5647509/best-spongebob-memes/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Michael Gold of ''The New York Times'' opined that because of the show's "high episode count" and that it was "so ubiquitous at the beginning of the 21st century", ''SpongeBob SquarePants'' became "easy meme fodder".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Gold |first1=Michael |date=May 2, 2018 |title=SpongeBob SquarePants Is 20 Now, and a Favorite Meme |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/01/arts/spongebob-squarepants-stephen-hillenburg.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190507221633/https://www.nytimes.com/2019/05/01/arts/spongebob-squarepants-stephen-hillenburg.html |archive-date=May 7, 2019 |access-date=August 31, 2022 |website=The New York Times}}</ref>

Among the show's most popular memes are the [[mocking SpongeBob]] meme, referring to an [[image macro]] from the episode "[[Little Yellow Book]]",<ref>{{cite web |author=Madison Malone Kircher |date=May 17, 2017 |title=WhAt Is Up WiTh ThAt WeIrD, NeW SpOnGeBoB MeMe? |url=https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2017/05/what-is-the-mocking-spongebob-capitalized-letters-chicken-meme.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231030063240/https://nymag.com/intelligencer/2017/05/what-is-the-mocking-spongebob-capitalized-letters-chicken-meme.html |archive-date=October 30, 2023 |access-date=October 30, 2023 |work=[[New York (magazine)|Intelligencer]]}}</ref> an image of Spongebob appearing exhausted in the episode "[[Nature Pants]]",<ref>{{cite web |last1=Wheeler |first1=André-Naquian |date=April 27, 2018 |title=The 'Tired Spongebob' Meme Captures Our Cultural Exhaustion |url=https://i-d.co/article/the-tired-spongebob-meme-captures-our-cultural-exhaustion/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250531070807/https://i-d.co/article/the-tired-spongebob-meme-captures-our-cultural-exhaustion/ |archive-date=May 31, 2025 |access-date=May 12, 2025 |website=i-D |publisher=Vice |language=en}}</ref> and a particularly disheveled illustration of Squidward from "[[Squid's Day Off]]".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Bryan |first1=Chloe |date=April 8, 2018 |title=Why is SpongeBob so damn meme-able? |url=https://mashable.com/article/spongebob-memes-explained |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221004005413/https://mashable.com/article/spongebob-memes-explained |archive-date=October 4, 2022 |access-date=August 31, 2022 |website=Mashable |language=en}}</ref>

Fans of the show have created various pages replicating Bikini Bottom News, a news show within the ''SpongeBob'' universe, with versions of the anchors Realistic Fish Head and Perch Perkins generated with [[Artificial intelligence art|artificial intelligence]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=January 25, 2024 |title=The rise of the TikTok news anchor |url=https://www.economist.com/united-states/2024/01/25/the-rise-of-the-tiktok-news-anchor |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241007195921/https://www.economist.com/united-states/2024/01/25/the-rise-of-the-tiktok-news-anchor |archive-date=October 7, 2024 |access-date=October 24, 2024 |newspaper=The Economist |issn=0013-0613}}</ref>

